                        Description = "To: mariapa@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\nBody:\nGrazzie!\nMartín Arévalo de León | Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 | www.unops.org Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Tue, Sep 30, 2025 at 3:14 PM Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org> wrote:\nFYI\n\n\nMaria Cristina Palamini | Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 |\nSkype: mcpalamini |Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\nDate: Tue, 30 Sept 2025 at 13:54\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\nCc: Pham, HangThiThanh (FAORAP) <HangThiThanh.Pham@fao.org>, Liao, Chongguang (FAORAP) <Chongguang.Liao@fao.org>, Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>, Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>, Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>, Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>, Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>, Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>, Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>, Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>, Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>, Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nDear YurieThanks to you and all FAO colleagues for the active participation. I hope the session was useful.I will respond to your questions within the next few days.Kind RegardsCristina\n\n\nMaria Cristina Palamini | Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand | Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 |\nSkype: mcpalamini |Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Tue, 30 Sept 2025 at 12:34, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina\n \nMany thanks for today’s meeting with FAO country offices.\n \nGrateful to receive your feedback on the list of questions that Zette shared.\nAlso, look forward to receiving the PPT.\n \nBest wishes, Yurie\n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Saturday, September 27, 2025 10:09\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Pham, HangThiThanh (FAORAP) <HangThiThanh.Pham@fao.org>; Liao, Chongguang (FAORAP) <Chongguang.Liao@fao.org>; Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>; Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>;\n Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>; Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>; Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Yurie\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find here linked a\n\nrevised draft of the FAO-UNOPS Regional Agreement.\n\n\n \n\n\nKindly note, we have included the possibility to receive Implementation support in the areas of Project implementation, Advisory, Grant Management, and Infrastructure\nat a fixed fee of 5.3% (indirect cost only).\n\n\n \n\n\nAs offering these services is more complex than HR and Procurement - which can be offered through a simple Request for Services - we have included a provision that they be subject to a separate\n agreement detailing the respective responsibility and support from both parties. At the same time, we are working with our HQ trying to explore ways to further simplify how FAO could engage UNOPS for these services, including the development of standard templates,\n which we will share with you, once finalised.\n\n\n \n\n\nI look forward to our session next Tuesday and to hearing feedback from FAO offices. \n\n\n\nIn the meantime, could you kindly let me know if your legal office has provided any comment on the Agreement we shared earlier,\n which already coveres HR and Procurement?\n\n\n \n\n\nWishing you a great week-end.\n\n\nBest Regards,\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\n\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 2 Sept 2025 at 11:15, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina,\n \nPlease note that the attached version was shared with FAO HQ and received a green light to proceed with finalization as the document is the standard template for UNtoUN agreement\n as per \nUN2UN-Transfer-Agreement-Template-FINAL-3-June-2021.pdf\n \nBest wishes, Yurie\n \n\nFrom: Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, August 1, 2025 17:42\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects\n\n \n\n\n\nHi Yurie \n\n\nthe inclusion of FTAs will need to be 1) agreed with your HQ and 2) justified (in terms of efficiency, cost, speed etc) in order for\n my HQ to agree.\n\n\nI can help draft a justification, if needed. Please let me know once you discuss with your HQ.\n\n\nRegards and have a great week-end\n\n\nCristina\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nMaria Cristina Palamini\n| Head of Programme - South East Asia and Pacific Multi-Country Office (EAPMCO) - Asia-Pacific\n Region| 14th Floor 208 Wireless Road Building, Lumphini, Bangkok 10330 - Bangkok, Thailand\n| Tel: +66 2 288 2657 | Mob: +66 98 246 2657 | Skype: mcpalamini\n|\n\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, 1 Aug 2025 at 17:35, Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Cristina\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for your message and the revised draft agreement. I'll use this version to discuss with HQ colleagues.\n\n\n \n\n\nI understood that if we want to include FTE personnel in the agreement, HQ level discussion and agreement, especially from HR team, is required.\n\n\n \n\n\nBest wishes, Yurie\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Maria\n PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\nSent: 01 August 2025 16:32\n\nTo: Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>\n\nCc: Zhao, Wei (FAORAP) <Wei.Zhao@fao.org>; Karki, Sameer (OCB) <Sameer.Karki@fao.org>; Trangthu NGUYEN <trangthun@unops.org>;\n Thazin AUNG <thazina@unops.org>; Muhomediev, Ilhom (CSLP) <Ilhom.Muhomediev@fao.org>; Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>;\n Samina KADWANI <saminak@unops.org>; Jennifer ANKROM <jennifera@unops.org>; Azusa CHIBA <azusac@unops.org>;\n Fatima AHMED <fatimaahm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Meeting with UNOPS team on executing GEF projects \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear FAO Colleagues,\n\n\n \n\n\nIn the interest of time, and as agreed separately with Yurie, I share a\n\nrevised draft AGREEMENT without the inclusion of Fixed Term Contracts, which requires additional HQ to HQ consultation.\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease feel free to share your comments. Grateful if you could work in revision mode so as to make it easier to track changes.\n\n\nThanks a lot for your patience