                new (
                    "00TQx00000SIQVSMA5",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Meeting invite: Exchange on EU collaboration ahead of Jorge’s trip to Brussels",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-03-17").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Meeting invite: Exchange on EU collaboration ahead of Jorge’s trip to Brussels",
                        Description = "To: danielgi@unops.org\nCC: saminak@unops.org; sarane@unops.org; charlesc@unops.org; clarag@unops.org; elizavetaz@unops.org; jeromedt@unops.org; laetitiak@unops.org; mariacarmenco@unops.org; nicholasg@unops.org; nitayav@unops.org; sanjaym@unops.org; yoogyoungk@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Meeting invite: Exchange on EU collaboration ahead of Jorge’s trip to Brussels\nBody:\nhi DanielA few points to sum up from Afghanistan for your meetings with Eric and other EU colleagues:\nEU:Firstly, we would like to convey our heartfelt condolences on the passing of EU former charge d'affaires to Afghanistan Raffaella Iodice.  She was a force of nature and \"an inspiring example of commitment to the rights and dignity of Afghan women\".  The Executive Director met with Raffealla during his mission to Afghanistan last yearwe currently do not have direct funding from EU and have not historically had any directly EU funded projects in Afghanistanhowever, EU contribute to the ARTF (Afghanistan Resilience Trust Fund) which funds our largest and flagship Community Resilience and Livelihoods Project CRLP (US$420m of ARTF and IDA funding via the WB) and the Water Emergency Relief Project WERP (US$39m of ARTF funding via WB).EC/EU was one of the largest contributors to the ARTF prior to 2021, contributing approx. US$1.15bn Since the change of regime in 2021, they contributed only US$18m and we understood this to be frozenHowever, I note that the only donor contributions received into the fund this year (2025 so far) actually come from the EU at US$30.92mIt would be interesting to know what is happening with the EU funding for ARTFAlthough the EU have not generally been that interested in meeting with UNOPS, this has recently changed with invites to contribute in workshops on Disaster Preparedness and Linking Drug Use Disorders Rehabilitation with Economic Livelihoods in AfghanistanOPPORTUNITIES:   the example from Myanmar (replicated now in UNOPS Lebanon for the Syria response) on pooled DG INTPA and DG ECHO funding into the EU Nexus Response Mechanism to work with civil society to operationalise the humanitarian-development-peac nexus is something that we would like to explore in Afghanistan.  UNOPS manages grants and procurement in line with the EU-set strategy.  This is something we could definitely replicate in Afghanistan.ECHO:ECHO has been very supportive of UNOPS, especially in funding the AWAAZ inter-agency humanitarian call centre managed by UNOPS since 2018 (Afghanistan’s first nationwide humanitarian call centre developed as a joint initiative between multiple UN agencies and partners (AHF, ECHO, Japan, UNWomen, UNFPA, UNDP, IOM, WFP, UNHCR).Awaaz recently hit a milestone of 500k calls answered (20% from female callers).ECHO actively support both by funding directly and advocating for other agencies and NGOs to be using Awaaz as their primary grievance mechanismECHO this week approved US$1m of funding for 2025.we are very grateful for the continued support of ECHOPlease let me know if you need any clarification or further informationNickG\nNick Gardner | Country Director & Representative | Afghanistan Country Office (AFCO) | Kabul, Afghanistan | Tel: +93 72 889 6345 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter | www.unops.org\n\nOn Mon, Mar 17, 2025 at 1:12 PM Daniel GIOREV <danielgi@unops.org> wrote:\nThank you colleagues! Well received and well read.\nOn Fri, 14 Mar 2025 at 04:35, Sara Austin NETZER <sarane@unops.org> wrote:\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n Meeting invite: Exchange on EU collaboration ahead of Jorge’s trip to Brussels   Dear colleagues,\nAs mentioned, please find our draft Myanmar approach to Team Europe. Looking forward to your thoughts and feedback. \nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1RtBrmD7muClPqDZA5-qM0wUzaccWd97R3HCmQgGXPo8/edit?usp=sharing Join with Google MeetMeeting linkmeet.google.com/dqx-jxnr-gfjJoin by phone(US) +1 636-707-2768 \nPIN: 452768444\n\nMore phone numbers\nMeeting invite: Exchange on EU collaboration ahead of Jorge’s trip to BrusselsThursday Mar 13, 2025 ⋅ 2:30pm – 3:30pm (Myanmar Time)Dear colleagues,\n\nThis meeting is called at the request of the Executive Office to exchange on EU collaboration ahead of Jorge’s trip to Brussels (17-19 March) and the EU Cooperation Days the following week. The objective is to brief the Executive Office on the EU portfolio in our region and for the Executive Office to update us on the partnership with the EU and discuss insights on potential areas for deeper engagement.\nLooking forward to seeing you all at the discussion.GuestsNitaya VATANAKOVIT - organizerElizaveta ZALKIND - creatorDaniel GIOREVNicholas Mark GARDNERNicholas GEORGESanjay MATHURCharles Rochford CALLANANSara Austin NETZERMariacarmen COLITTISamina KADWANIClara MATHIEU GOTCHJerome DE THYSEBAERTLaetitia KRAUSYoo Gyoung KIM",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000SIQVSMA5",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "yoogyoungk@unops.org", "elizavetaz@unops.org", "danielgi@unops.org", "sarane@unops.org", "jeromedt@unops.org", "saminak@unops.org", "nicholasg@unops.org", "nitayav@unops.org", "sanjaym@unops.org", "mariacarmenco@unops.org", "charlesc@unops.org", "laetitiak@unops.org", "clarag@unops.org" },
