                new (
                    "00TQx00000P8vZ8MAJ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Notes from informal meeting with Danish MFA ahead of the Annual EB session, June 2-5",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-05-13").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Notes from informal meeting with Danish MFA ahead of the Annual EB session, June 2-5",
                        Description = "To: hilaryb@unops.org; rahulm@unops.org; freyavg@unops.org; thomasl@unops.org; markuso@unops.org; carolinapo@unops.org\nCC: kirstined@unops.org; marijev@unops.org; jakobt@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; kerriet@unops.org; oonaa@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Notes from informal meeting with Danish MFA ahead of the Annual EB session, June 2-5\nBody:\nDear colleagues, \nThis morning I briefly met informally with the working level at the Danish MFA, who is preparing the Danish position for the upcoming Annual EB session. \nWhile the Danes noted that they did not yet study all the documents for the EB session, they offered their help and support if there were particular issues important to UNOPS.  I noted their kind offer and pointed towards our desire for the EB to 1) acknowledge the closure of the Comprehensive Response Plan, 2) unlock funding for the implementation of the PID and 3) endorse UNOPS' approach to the next Strategic Plan, noting that UNOPS would not venture into new territories and stick to the original mandate as set out in Resolution 65/176 and subsequent EB decisions. \nThe Danes underlined that - like many other Member States - it would continue to be a key priority for Denmark to ensure that UNOPS would stick to its mandate of providing infrastructure, procurement and project management.  I assured the Danes that this would be the core message of the next Strategic Plan - while we would also work towards more outcome (rather than only output) based reporting and become mission driven to ensure a return to UN values.   \nAs for the independent third party review of the implementation of the CRP, the Danes noted the importance of maintaining momentum on aspects related to culture, as this was a key concern for many Member States. \nThe Danes were also keen on hearing UNOPS' views on the UN80  discussions. I referred to the statement given by the SG yesterday and noted that we would be pleased to continue to work on the implementation capacity of partners - both the UN and other partners. I also noted that UNOPS was supportive of a strengthened RC system (or a sort of One Stop UN Shop) as this was a way to distribute the tasks to the UN agencies best capable of handling the individual task. \n\n/Asbjørn\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000P8vZ8MAJ",
