                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: [EXTERNAL] SDC - UNOPS template contribution agreement",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-05-02").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: [EXTERNAL] SDC - UNOPS template contribution agreement",
                        Description = "To: martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch\nCC: guillaumele@unops.org; svene@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: [EXTERNAL] SDC - UNOPS template contribution agreement\nBody:\nDear Martin\nGood to hear from you (we were worried !!)  No need to sign Framework Agreements from our side - we just date and log as final. This will be used as a template going forward, with project by project agreements that will be signed by our country level colleagues.Please let us know when Pascal has validated these last minor changes.You and I can be in touch in due course to discuss the communication on the revised FA with our country teams.\nThanks for this great collaboration and best wishes - to all - for a restful weekend. :)Louise\n\nOn Fri, 2 May 2025 at 08:56, Borgeaud Martin EDA BORGM <martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear colleagues,\n \nI apologize for not being able to attend this morning session. That said, the latest modifications are fine to me and I sent the final\n version to my colleague Pascal as he is responsible for validating all changes. I am not sure we need to meet since the latest changes were very minor?\n\n \nThe only question I have is whether we should sign the document electronically? What is the practice from your end (as for SDC, we could\n do electronical signature)? \n \nBest regards,\nMartin\n \n \n\nFrom: Guillaume LEMENEZ <guillaumele@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, May 2, 2025 8:50 AM\n\nTo: Borgeaud Martin EDA BORGM <martin.borgeaud@eda.admin.ch>; Louise Jocelyn LEECH <louisel@unops.org>; Sven ECKERT <svene@unops.org>\n\nSubject: [EXTERNAL] SDC - UNOPS template contribution agreement\n\n \n\n\nDear All, \n\n\n \n\n\nIn preparation for our meeting this morning, please find attached the latest version of our template.  I have accepted all changes in the last version received from Martin on 29 April and marked outstanding points to be cleared in track\n changes, namely: \n\n\n \n\n\nRe. to EB decision 2023/26 in special condition 2.35 (I adjusted to ref. to say \" without prejudice to following decisions\" - you will let me know if this is ok); \n\n\n \n\n\nDeletion of excluded general condition in Annex II - General conditions; \n\n\n \n\n\nMore generic reference to relevant SDC focal points when we need to inform SDC if an allegation reported through relevant channels could have a significant impact on the SDC/UNOPS partnership. \n\n\n \n\n\nTalk to you in a few minutes. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest regards, \n\n\nGuillaume\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-----------------------------\nGuillaume Lemenez\n| Legal Advisor, Team Lead for the AFR/ECR/GPO (GVA) team, Commercial Law Practice, Legal Group | Geneva, Switzerland | Tel: +41791359187 |\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. |\nwww.unops.org",
