                    "00TQx00000OFKS5MAP",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-04-21").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio",
                        Description = "To: Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org\nCC: Sandra.Corsi@fao.org; Arianna.Dottori@fao.org; Jeffrey.Griffin@fao.org; Yurie.Naito@fao.org; Maude.VeyretPicot@fao.org; evelynebak@unops.org; martina@unops.org; entelas@unops.org; elenage@unops.org; edrissr@unops.org; KatrinL@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\nBody:\nDear Tommaso,Let me briefly introduce myself: I’m Nuno Rodrigues Paulo, Head of the UNOPS Office for Angola and based in Angola.Our team is finalizing the initial drafts for the requested support modalities — including full implementation, the 12-month launch package, and the back-on-track option.Before we finalize and share these for discussion in the coming days, I’d like to seek a few key clarifications to ensure the proposals are fully aligned with FAO’s expectations and implementation framework.To refine our costing, scope, and partnership approach, we would appreciate your guidance on the following:A. On Budget FlexibilityCould FAO confirm whether there is flexibility to reprogram existing budget lines (e.g., national consultancy, operational costs) toward UNOPS-delivered servicesIs FAO aware of any additional sources of funding or co-financing (e.g., bilateral contributions, parallel FAO resources, or pipeline funds) that could be mobilized to support UNOPS-delivered services if needed?  B. On Execution ModalityCould you confirm whether FAO envisions UNOPS support as a means to strengthen and complement the national PMU — for example, through hosting selected functions, providing fiduciary safeguards, or offering technical backstopping — rather than fully taking over its structure  If a 12-month launch package is pursued should UNOPS lead the recruitment of 4–5 key PMU positions only (technical, fiduciary), or is there an expectation to temporarily host these roles under UNOPS contracts during the first year? \n\nDoes FAO foresee the 12-month package as a steppingstone to full implementation by UNOPS, or as a standalone support track leading back to national execution?C. On Component PrioritizationAre there specific project outputs or components currently considered at risk, or of particular strategic importance, where UNOPS support would add the most value.D. On Reporting and Fiduciary RolesWould FAO retain overall reporting responsibilities to GEF, or would UNOPS be expected to assume both technical and financial reporting roles?These clarifications will allow us to finalize tailored budgets and support options for FAO's review.Thank you again for the opportunity to collaborate. We look forward to working together to ensure a pragmatic and effective delivery model.\nCom os melhores cumprimentos,Nuno RODRIGUES PAULO | Head of Country Office | UNOPS Angola, Cabo Verde, Sao Tomé e Principe  |  Luanda, Angola Tel: +244 928443147 | www.unops.org  Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube.\n\nOn Fri, 11 Apr 2025 at 10:22, Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI understand. Thank you.\n \n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, April 11, 2025 11:20 AM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nCc: Corsi, Sandra (OCB) <Sandra.Corsi@fao.org>; Dottori, Arianna (OCBD) <Arianna.Dottori@fao.org>; Griffin, Jeffrey (OCB) <Jeffrey.Griffin@fao.org>; Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; VeyretPicot, Maude (OCB) <Maude.VeyretPicot@fao.org>; Nuno\n Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org>; Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Evelyne BAKAJI LUMBALA <evelynebak@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>; Edriss RIFFAT <edrissr@unops.org>; Katrin LICHTENBERG <KatrinL@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nDear Tommaso:\n\n\n \n\n\nAs you may understand it's not a fixed fee format we manage for these requirements, the team is already working in the preparation of preliminary budget proposals, considering the information at hand.\n\n\nAs soon as we have them they will be shared with you and your team.\n\n\n \n\n\nCheers and have a great week-end.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Fri, Apr 11, 2025 at 11:16 AM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nMany Thanks Martin. This helps a lot.\n\n \nWe stand ready to discuss the Angola budgets  at your signal. Hopefully by Wednesday next week as I will be out thur/fri\n \nThanks\n \nTommaso\n\n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, April 11, 2025 8:42 AM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nCc: Corsi, Sandra (OCB) <Sandra.Corsi@fao.org>; Dottori, Arianna (OCBD) <Arianna.Dottori@fao.org>; Griffin, Jeffrey (OCB) <Jeffrey.Griffin@fao.org>;\n Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; VeyretPicot, Maude (OCB) <Maude.VeyretPicot@fao.org>; Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org>;\n Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Evelyne BAKAJI LUMBALA <evelynebak@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>;\n Edriss RIFFAT <edrissr@unops.org>; Katrin LICHTENBERG <KatrinL@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nDear Tommaso:\n\n\n \n\n\n\nAs you already know, most of our work in support of GEF projects is managed by WEC but there are some exemptions.\n\n\n \n\n\n1. UNOPS manages the GEF project, ‘Implementing the strategic action programme for the South China Sea and Gulf of Thailand’, on\n behalf of UNEP. Working closely with the governments of Cambodia, China, Indonesia, Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam, the project aims to protect natural habitats, improve planning based on scientific knowledge, and encourage cooperation between countries\n in managing coastal areas.\n\n\n2. UNOPS also manages the GEF project, ‘Protecting and restoring the ocean’s natural capital,\n building resilience and supporting region-wide Investments for sustainable blue socio-economic development (PROCARIBE+)’ on behalf of UNDP.\n\n\n3. The GEF Small Grants Programme (SGP) is\n a global program implemented by UNDP-GEF and executed by UNOPS. UNOPS has been the implementing partner for the SGP since its inception in 1992. The SGP is a Corporate GEF program that provides grants to community-based organizations and NGOs working on environmental\n conservation and sustainable development.\n\n\nUNOPS's role in the SGP is to provide a range of services, including:\n\n·\nLegal framework: UNOPS provides the legal framework for the SGP, ensuring that it operates in accordance with international standards.\n\n·\nGrant management services: UNOPS manages the grant application process, including reviewing proposals, awarding grants, and monitoring grant implementation.\n\n·\nOperations support: UNOPS provides operational support to SGP projects, including financial management, procurement, travel, and other administrative\n services.\n\n·\nPersonnel recruitment: UNOPS assists with the recruitment of staff for SGP projects.\n\n·\nProcurement: UNOPS helps with the procurement of goods and services for SGP projects.\n\n·\nFinancial management: UNOPS manages the SGP's finances, including accounting, budgeting, and reporting.\n\n4. UNOPS is the executing agency for the GEF \"Biodiversity conservation, sustainable land management\n and enhanced water security in Lake Tanganyika basin\" for which UNEP is the implementing agency. The project aims to enhance transboundary cooperation and SAP implementation through sustainable fisheries co-management, biodiversity conservation and restoration\n of degraded landscapes in selected key biodiversity of Lake Tanganyika.\n\n\n \n\n\nIt's also worth mentioning that UNOPS hosts and manages a number of multi-stakeholder climate funds and initiatives\n such as the Initiative for Climate Action Transparency and the NDC Partnership.\n\n\n \n\n\nI'm looping in our colleague Katrin Lichtenberg, who in light of her experience with the management of GEF funds may\n contribute to this effort of setting a general collaboration framework for implementation / execution.\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Apr 9, 2025 at 12:02 PM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nOne more input that would be useful for our meeting would be an example of an existing UNOPS budget with a UNDP or UNEP GEF project… so to also understand\n how they have presented it. \n \nI can retrieve it in the GEF portal if you share the GEF ID or also  project title +  country\n\n \nThanks\n \nTommaso\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB)\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, April 9, 2025 11:59 AM\n\nTo: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\nCc: Corsi, Sandra (OCB) <Sandra.Corsi@fao.org>; Dottori, Arianna (OCBD) <Arianna.Dottori@fao.org>; Griffin, Jeffrey (OCB) <Jeffrey.Griffin@fao.org>;\n Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; VeyretPicot, Maude (OCB) <Maude.VeyretPicot@fao.org>; Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org>;\n Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Evelyne BAKAJI LUMBALA <evelynebak@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>;\n Edriss RIFFAT <edrissr@unops.org>\n\nSubject: RE: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n\n \nGreat thanks\n\n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, April 9, 2025 11:05 AM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nCc: Corsi, Sandra (OCB) <Sandra.Corsi@fao.org>; Dottori, Arianna (OCBD) <Arianna.Dottori@fao.org>; Griffin, Jeffrey (OCB) <Jeffrey.Griffin@fao.org>;\n Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; VeyretPicot, Maude (OCB) <Maude.VeyretPicot@fao.org>; Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org>;\n Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Evelyne BAKAJI LUMBALA <evelynebak@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>;\n Edriss RIFFAT <edrissr@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nDear Tomasso:\n\n\n \n\n\nWe`ll make sure we get you a proposal considering all the information at hand.\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Apr 9, 2025 at 10:55 AM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Martin,\n\n \nForgive me this e-mail -  has fallen through the cracks.\n\n \nFriday or Monday morning would be an ideal time for us to meet.  But it would be good if the UNOPS team can come already with a proposal please, at\n least the one for the full execution of the project budgets shared.  We would ideally like to avoid sitting in another meeting without a draft budget in front of us, please.\n\n \nI’m just out of a meeting with our full project task Force for Angola and there is strong interest on working through UNOPS, our FAORs sees also no\n major obstacles with the Ministry. \n \nWe look forward to move ahead at speed.\n\n \nThanks\n \nTommaso\n\n \n \n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday, April 4, 2025 10:42 AM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nCc: Corsi, Sandra (OCB) <Sandra.Corsi@fao.org>; Dottori, Arianna (OCBD) <Arianna.Dottori@fao.org>; Griffin, Jeffrey (OCB) <Jeffrey.Griffin@fao.org>;\n Naito, Yurie (OCB) <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; VeyretPicot, Maude (OCB) <Maude.VeyretPicot@fao.org>; Nuno Miguel RODRIGUES PAULO <rodriguespaulon@unops.org>;\n Entela SULA <entelas@unops.org>; Evelyne BAKAJI LUMBALA <evelynebak@unops.org>; Elena GEORGALLA <elenage@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nDear Tomasso:\n\n\n \n\n\nWe have contacted our Angola Team, here in copy, and would like to have the meeting between your team and ours, so we all understand the scope of the programme and be able to respond\n accordingly to each dynamic, considering particularities you may to signal.\n\n\nPlease make a proposal of when would that meeting be possible to check on agendas.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Apr 2, 2025 at 3:47 PM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Martin,\n\n \nAgain thank you very much for the productive meeting.\n\n \nAs agreed, please find attached the budgets for 2 projects in Angola for which we are keen to explore UNOP’s service costs. There is a third project\n coming in June for which we don’t have the budget yet. \nWe are also attaching an exercise we are doing for Timor lest with Akira although focused on HR services.\n\n \nGrateful if you could put us in contact with the UNOPS Africa Office for a simulation for the following options scenarios/services:\n\n\n\nFull execution of the 2 projects\nrecruitment of all international consultants only\n12 months project Launch package,  including : inception workshop, preparation of technical specification for procurement processes, TORs for PMU (4-5 consultants), tailored capacity\n building on moderate/high risk partner – see example moderate risk HACT capacity assessment from South Sudan attached to identify recurrent capacity gaps. Please pretend that was in Angola.  We have to limit the costs of these capacity building services in\n order to comply with GEF rules which leave limited space for this support, could be the equivalent 30- 40 days of work of a consultant)\n\nBack on track approach including capacity building as per point 3, takeover of all subcontracts/sub- partnering services, procurement services and HR. This can be for 12 months or for\n the entire duration of the project after a certain point. \n \nWe are available to further clarify the request to the team in writing or in a meeting if needed.\n\n \nThanks and we look forward to hearing from you and colleagues\n \nTommaso and  Arianna\n \n\n-----Original Appointment-----\n\nFrom: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) \n\nSent: Tuesday, April 1, 2025 2:55 PM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB); Martin AREVALO\n\nCc: Corsi, Sandra (OCB); Dottori, Arianna (OCBD)\n\nSubject: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\nWhen: Wednesday, April 2, 2025 2:00 PM-2:30 PM (UTC+01:00) Amsterdam, Berlin, Bern, Rome, Stockholm, Vienna.\n\nWhere: D661\n\n \nForgive me – I meant 2 not 3.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n \nUNOPS Overview:\n\nGoogle Slides.\n \n \n_____________________________________________\n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, April 1, 2025 2:38 PM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n \n\n\nCheers Tomasso,\n\n\n \n\n\nDon't worry. I understand.\n\n\nWe can do it tomorrow at 2pm.\n\n\nMeet you at D661, and yes I'm at the FAO building.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Apr 1, 2025 at 2:07 PM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nMy apologies  Martin – here things shift quickly and I can’t anymore at 4. It can be 3 PM or 5 PM..\n\n \notherwise tomorrow, if you prefer. Either 2 PM or 4PM\n\n \nare you in FAO building?\n\nWe could meet in my room D661…\n \nMany thanks\n\n \nTommaso \n\n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, April 1, 2025 12:35 PM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nCheers Tomasso,\n\n\n \n\n\n4 pm today is alright with me.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Apr 1, 2025 at 10:01 AM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Martin,\n\n \nHow about this afternoon at 4PM?\n\n \nThanks\n \nTommaso\n\n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, March 27, 2025 3:41 PM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nCiao Tomasso.\n\n\nMi dispiace sapere che oggi sei stato malato.\n\n\nLasciami sapere quando potrei trovarci.\n\n\n \n\n\nCheers,\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Mar 25, 2025 at 3:24 PM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nCiao – thanks\n \nThursday at 3.30?\n\n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, March 25, 2025 3:21 PM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nCiao Tomasso.\n\n\nLet me know when you want to follow up on this.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Mar 25, 2025 at 1:58 PM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nPerfect! thanks\n \n\nFrom: Edriss RIFFAT <edrissr@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Tuesday, March 25, 2025 1:34 PM\n\nTo: Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n\nCc: Bergigui, MohamedFouad (OCBD) <Mohamed.Bergigui@fao.org>;\n Basaran, Kaan (REU) <Kaan.Basaran@fao.org>; Gonzalez, Hernan\n (OCB) <Hernan.Gonzalez@fao.org>; Becker, Aaron (FAORAP)\n <Aaron.Becker@fao.org>; VeyretPicot, Maude (OCB) <Maude.VeyretPicot@fao.org>;\nmartina@unops.org; Dionyssia GEKA <dionyssiag@unops.org>;\n Dottori, Arianna (OCBD) <Arianna.Dottori@fao.org>; Corsi,\n Sandra (OCB) <Sandra.Corsi@fao.org>; Naito, Yurie (OCB)\n <Yurie.Naito@fao.org>; Damen, Beau (FAORAP) <Beau.Damen@fao.org>;\n Pham, HangThiThanh (FAORAP) <HangThiThanh.Pham@fao.org>;\n Akira MORETTO <akiram@unops.org>; Ffion CONLON <ffionc@unops.org>;\n Ada SAFANOVA <adas@unops.org>; Katrin LICHTENBERG <katrinl@unops.org>;\n Maria PALAMINI <mariapa@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\n \n\n\nDear Tommaso,\n\n\n \n\n\nWe will make a presentation about our services which will cover pricing, among other things. After that, we will take your questions. \n\n\n \n\n\nBest, Edriss\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, Mar 25, 2025 at 7:05 AM Vicario, Tommaso (OCB) <Tommaso.Vicario@fao.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nHi Riffat,\n\n \nWe will have mostly questions on services available  and related to cost recovery … in case you are able to loop in someone from the finance/operational team.\n\n \nPls Disregard if already done\n😊 \n \nThanks and see you soon\n \nTommaso Vicario\nPolicy, Monitoring and Liaison Lead\n\nFAO GEF Coordination Unit\nOffice of Climate Change, Biodiversity and Environment\n– D661\nTel: +39 0657052772\n \n \n \n \n\n-----Original Appointment-----\n\nFrom: Bergigui, MohamedFouad (OCBD) <Mohamed.Bergigui@fao.org>\n\n\nSent: Wednesday, March 12, 2025 10:37 AM\n\nTo: Bergigui, MohamedFouad (OCBD); Bergigui, MohamedFouad (OCBD); Edriss RIFFAT; Vicario, Tommaso (OCB); Basaran, Kaan (REU); Gonzalez, Hernan (OCB); Becker, Aaron (FAORAP); VeyretPicot, Maude (OCB);\nmartina@unops.org\n\nCc: Dionyssia GEKA; Dottori, Arianna (OCBD); Corsi, Sandra (OCB); Naito, Yurie (OCB); Damen, Beau (FAORAP); Pham, HangThiThanh (FAORAP); Akira MORETTO; Ffion CONLON; Ada SAFANOVA; Katrin LICHTENBERG; Maria PALAMINI\n\nSubject: UNOPS value proposition to support FAO's GEF portfolio\n\nWhen: Tuesday, March 25, 2025 2:00 PM-3:00 PM (UTC+01:00) Amsterdam, Berlin, Bern, Rome, Stockholm, Vienna.\n\nWhere: Microsoft Teams Meeting\n\n \nHi Riffat, as discussed, let us know if the proposed timing works, 9am NY / 2pm Rome / 8pm BKK (apologies to our colleagues in BKK, we can alternatively gather your inputs upfront\n and record the meeting). Please feel free to share the invite with UNOPS colleagues who will be joining. Thank you all.\n \n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________\n\n\nMicrosoft\n Teams\nNeed help?\n\n\n\nJoin\n the meeting now\n\n\n\nMeeting\n ID: 334\n 105 607 620\n\n\n\nPasscode:\nkq9dP7Kj\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFor\n organizers: Meeting\n options\n\n\n\n________________________________________________________________________________",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000OFKS5MAP",
