                new (
                    "00TQx00000O4oGfMAJ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: UNS Procurement Panel - CODEWAY2025",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-04-16").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: UNS Procurement Panel - CODEWAY2025",
                        Description = "To: martina@unops.org\nCC: isabella.ambroglini@gmail.com; l.ridori@fieraroma.it; JeromeDT@unops.org; anarom@unops.org; marcusm@unops.org; filippo.lonardo@esteri.it\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: UNS Procurement Panel - CODEWAY2025\nBody:\nDear Mr. Arevalo,\nThank you very much for your message and for confirming the possibility of remote participation. I will share the name of our speaker as soon as possible.\nIn the meanwhile, for any further communication, please feel free to reach out to me.\nBest regards,\nCristina\n \n \nCristina Franchini (She/Her)\nExternal Relations Associate\nUNHCR Representation for Italy, the Holy See and San Marino\n\nOffice: +39 06 8021 2511 | Mobile +39 349 5637026\nVia Leopardi 24, 00185 Roma, Italy \n\nwww.unhcr.org|https://www.unhcr.org/it/\nTwitter|Facebook|Instagram\n\n\n\n \n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, April 14, 2025 12:21 PM\n\nTo: Cristina Franchini <franchin@unhcr.org>\n\nCc: Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <JeromeDT@unops.org>; Ana-Paula ROMERO <anarom@unops.org>; Marcus MCKAY <marcusm@unops.org>; Isabella Ambroglini <isabella.ambroglini@gmail.com>; Luisa Ridori <l.ridori@fieraroma.it>; Lonardo Filippo <filippo.lonardo@esteri.it>\n\nSubject: Re: UNS Procurement Panel - CODEWAY2025\n\n \n\n\nDear Cristina:\n\n\n \n\n\nWe have been informed that exceptionally, UNHCR will be able to participate remotely, both in the Panel discussion and then in the following B2B sessions to be held with private enterprises. For this B2B session, please refer to Isabela\n Ambroglini and Luisa Ridori herein copied, for the specifics.\n\n\n \n\n\nCheers,\n\n\n \n\n\nI'm copying my colleagues organizing and structuring this even so you and the officer to participate (please refer it to us as soon as possible) can loop in smoothly.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \n\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, Apr 14, 2025 at 11:27 AM Cristina Franchini <franchin@unhcr.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Mr. Arevalo,\nI hope this email finds you well.\n\nI am writing to know if there are news about the possibility of participating in the procurement panel remotely.\nThanks a lot for your kind feedback,\n\nCristina\n \n \nCristina Franchini\n(She/Her)\nExternal Relations Associate\nUNHCR Representation for Italy, the Holy See and San Marino\n\nOffice: +39 06 8021 2511 | Mobile +39 349 5637026\nVia Leopardi 24, 00185 Roma, Italy\n\n\nwww.unhcr.org|https://www.unhcr.org/it/\nTwitter|Facebook|Instagram\n\n\n\n \n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Monday, April 7, 2025 9:46 AM\n\nTo: Cristina Franchini <franchin@unhcr.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNS Procurement Panel - CODEWAY2025\n\n \n\n\nDear Mrs Franchini,\n\n\n \n\n\nMy apologies for not responding appropriately.\n\n\nI'm checking with the organizers on the possibility of remote participation.\n\n\nI hope to get back on this with you today.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Apr 3, 2025 at 2:37 PM Cristina Franchini <franchin@unhcr.org>\n wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Martin,\nThank you for the reminder. I have sent an email to you and Filippo regarding remote participation, and I am not sure if you've had a chance to see it yet. I have reattached the\n email for your convenience. Would it be possible to arrange remote participation?\nThank you very much for your kind response.\nCristina\n\n \n \nCristina Franchini\n(She/Her)\nExternal Relations Associate\nUNHCR Representation for Italy, the Holy See and San Marino\n\nOffice: +39 06 8021 2511 | Mobile +39 349 5637026\nVia Leopardi 24, 00185 Roma, Italy\n\n\nwww.unhcr.org|https://www.unhcr.org/it/\nTwitter|Facebook|Instagram\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Thursday, April 3, 2025 11:41 AM\n\nTo: c.ziniel@unido.org;\nsnuvoli@unicef.org; Cristina Franchini <franchin@unhcr.org>;\ncorvagi@unhcr.org\n\nCc: Jerome DE THYSEBAERT <JeromeDT@unops.org>; Marcus MCKAY <marcusm@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: UNS Procurement Panel - CODEWAY2025\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from\nmartina@unops.org. \nLearn why this is important \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAttention: This email is from an external sender.\n Please be careful with any links or attachments. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear colleagues:\n\n\n \n\n\nHoping my message finds you well, I would like to request your confirmation for participation, or not, to the CODEWAY2025 session as per my previous message.\n\n\nThank you very much for your attention and your kind response.\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Mar 12, 2025 at 5:04 PM Martin AREVALO <martina@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear colleagues,\n\n\n \n\nFollowing the success of last year's event we are coordinating this crucial session at the request of the DGCS of MoFA. So this mail is to reach out to invite and explore your agency's\n interest and active collaboration.  \n\n \n\nThis year's session will be held on 14th May at 16:00, on the inauguration day of CODEWAY2025. We propose that the central focus should be on enhancing and increasing private\n sector participation in UN bidding processes.\n\n\n\n\nIn today's complex polycrisis world, with strained traditional aid models, engaging the private sector is vital for UN agencies to amplify our impact, build resilience, drive sustainable development, and leverage alternative funding streams. The private sector\n brings resources, innovation, and agility crucial for delivering sustainable solutions.\n\n·      \nThis session offers a unique opportunity to:\n\n·      \nExplore strategic partnerships with the private sector.\n\n·      \nDiscuss innovative approaches to mobilise private sector investment in our initiatives.\n\n·      \nConsider how to best leverage private sector innovation and agility in crisis situations.\n\n·      \nContribute to developing standardised frameworks for collaboration.\n\n\nGiven the current global landscape, where a continued increase in SDG plans and ODC engagement is not foreseen, fostering strong partnerships with the private sector is more critical\n than ever.\n\n\n\n\nCan I please invite you to reflect on these points and consider entry points for discussion or participation. Your valuable insights will be instrumental in structuring a compelling and impactful panel format.\n\n\n\n\nPlease confirm your agency's interest in participating, and we will share further details regarding collaborative opportunities and the agenda soon.\n\n\n\n\nWe look forward to a fruitful collaboration.\n\nSincerely,\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nMartín Arévalo de León\n| Representative and Head | Partnerships & Liaisons Group | Rome Liaison Office | Rome, Italy | Cel +39 344 778 3550 |\nwww.unops.org \nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
