                    new List<string> { "B0047" }
                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000NNobmMAD",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Update on process and first questions from the MFA",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-03-31").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Update on process and first questions from the MFA",
                        Description = "To: eb@tanacph.com\nCC: eleneag@unops.org; marysiaz@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Update on process and first questions from the MFA\nBody:\nHi Erik,\nThanks for sending over the clean version of the document.\nI've reviewed the MFA's comments and have addressed them in the attached document using track changes. I wanted to give you a brief overview of how I approached each point:\n1. Capacity building: I've added specific examples of capacity-building activities, clarified how they will be implemented, and specified the intended target groups. While I fully agree on the need to build local capacity for eg. procurement when delivering services, please consider that the main outcome of the project afterall is the delivery of the items procured and the infrastructure we build. We now have quite elaborate descriptions of capacity building activities in the document which is fine. But if capacity building becomes the main part of the project - it is an entirely different project we are discussing. Please consider this when reviewing the document again. \n2. Infrastructure projects: I've included language to ensure the project could also consider general social infrastructure, such as elderly care facilities and administrative service buildings - if they are identified during the prioritization process. \n3. Baselines: I can confirm that baselines, indicators and outputs will be established for each intervention in the Results Framework to gauge progress and measure impact - once the specific interventions have been identified. I have reinforced this - but please notice that this is already clearly stated in the second paragraph under \"results framework\". \nFinally I hope that in general we can avoid too many references to individual units within the Danish MFA (such as LÆRING, EUNABO, etc.) as this document constitutes an institutional level framework between the MFA, Ukraine and UNOPS. \nPlease take a look at the changes and let me know if you have any questions or further suggestions.\nPS - as today is a UN holiday my colleagues did not have a chance to review my suggestions yet. They may therefore come up with adjustments that we would have to incorporate. \nPlease do not hesitate to call me if there are any comments, suggestions, etc. \nBest,Asbjørn\n\nOn Fri, 28 Mar 2025 at 08:12, Erik Bryld <eb@tanacph.com> wrote:\nDear Asbjørn,\nSounds good. See attached.\n- Erik\nErik Bryld Managing DirectorTana Copenhagen \nPalægade 3, 4th \nDK-1261 Copenhagen K \nDenmark \n\nT  +45 3536 1915\nM +45 2557 9797\neb@tanacph.com \nwww.tanacopenhagen.com\n\n\nDen 28. mar. 2025 kl. 10.06 skrev Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>:\nHi Erik\nI will get back to you over the course of the weekend with this. \nWould you have a clean version of the document that I could work on? Or should I continue working in the last version (which contains quite a few TC)? \nI also have a few remarks from our legal department that I will include when reverting to you. \nBest,Asbjørn\nOn Fri, 28 Mar 2025 at 03:54, Erik Bryld <eb@tanacph.com> wrote:\nDear Asbjørn,\nThe MFA has updated the approval process for the Ukraine programme. We will now submit the drafts for pre-appraisal Tuesday next week. We will then edit the document together and there will then be a final appraisal in May.\nThe MFA has the following comments before we submit to pre-appraisal:\n1.    Capacity building (pgs. 3 and 7): The description of capacity-building activities is very generic. It would be useful if the sections could specify the type of capacity-building activities, how they will be implemented, and who will be targeted.  \n2.    Infrastructure projects – a general remark: All infrastructure efforts focus on three main sectors: education, healthcare and housing. Should the project also consider general social infrastructure? For example, a hromada could require support with (re)construction of elderly care facilities, administrative services buildings. I.e., the rehabilitation of facilities that are not under the three categories.  3.    Baselines: Is there a plan for placing baselines in the Results Framework? Without baselines it is not possible to gauge progress and thereby measure impact.  \nCan you get back to me on these three questions by Monday. On the last question I guess that the response is that baselines will be established for each project/investment?\n- Erik\n\nErik Bryld Managing DirectorTana Copenhagen \nPalægade 3, 4th \nDK-1261 Copenhagen K \nDenmark \n\nT  +45 3536 1915\nM +45 2557 9797\neb@tanacph.com \nwww.tanacopenhagen.com\n<Tana_logo_turkis_e-mailsignatur.jpg>\n\n\n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000NNobmMAD",
