                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-02-07").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UNOPS and Finland in Ethiopia",
                        Description = "To: pia.korpinen@gov.fi; asbjornb@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; workneshg@unops.org\nCC: \nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS and Finland in Ethiopia\nBody:\nDear Pia and Worke,\n\nI hope this message finds you well.\n\nDespite this being a busy period for everyone, I wanted to\ntake this opportunity to follow up on our meeting last December. We greatly\nappreciated the conversation and look forward to continuing our engagement in\n2025, with a view to establishing potential partnership opportunities in the\nfuture.\n\nWe would be happy to provide further information and meet\nfor follow-up consultations, particularly related to some of the areas of\ninterest and priority you highlighted in support of Finland's priorities in\nEthiopia, such as:\n\n·      \nRural economic development\n\n·      \nSustainable land/resource management\n\n·      \nDigital transformation and system support\n\n·      \nImproving WASH services\n\n·      \nStrengthening conditions for inclusive basic\neducation\n\nDuring our conversation, we also discussed potentially\ncomplementary support services we might offer to support your collaboration and\ninitiatives with relevant line ministries, such as providing procurement\nservices and advisory or accelerating projects/programs like the completion of\nthe mentioned four meteorology stations.\n\nMight you be available for a brief follow-up meeting next\nweek?\n\nWith my best wishes for a restful weekend ahead,\n\nSilke\nOn Wed, Dec 18, 2024 at 7:02 PM Silke Grundmann HANDLEY <silkeh@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Pia and Worke,\n\nThank you for the wonderful meeting last week with Asbjorn,\nNaimo, and myself, and for the very interesting discussion we had regarding\nUNOPS’ scope of work across the Humanitarian-Development-Peace Nexus in\nEthiopia, as well as learning about Finland’s thematic priorities and strategic\nvisions.\n\nThe UNOPS Ethiopia team looks forward to continuing our\nengagement in 2025, with a view to establishing potential partnership\nopportunities in the future. By leveraging UNOPS' mandate and capacities to\nprovide infrastructure, procurement, and multi-sectoral project management\nservices, we hope to support the advancement of Finland's priorities in\nEthiopia, particularly in rural economic development, sustainable land/resource\nmanagement, digital transformation and system support, improving WASH services,\nand strengthening the conditions for inclusive basic education (kindly see the\nattached capacity statements).We would be interested in follow-up conversations related to complementary support services we might offer to facilitate in support of your partnership with relevant line ministries, such as providing procurement services and advisory or accelerating projects/programs like the completion of the mentioned four meteorology stations. As noted, UNOPS can offer to conduct a diagnostic assessment as a first instance, to determine root causes for project performance issues, benchmark practices, map required skills for the project in recovery; and re-plan projects to deliver expected results.As discussed during our conversation, I am attaching a snapshot overview of UNOPS’ multi-sectoral efforts supporting reconstruction, recovery, and stabilization across Tigray, providing a key opportunity for scale-up and expansion, supporting the region's pathway towards recovery and peace.Through diligent data collection and assessment work, UNOPS has gathered a comprehensive understanding of infrastructure damages, recovery needs, and priority areas across the Tigray Region, including the WASH and education sectors. We would be happy to have a follow-up conversation in this regard.On behalf of UNOPS, I wish you and your families a restful and peaceful end-of-year vacation, and I sincerely look forward to continuing our conversation in 2025.With my warmest regards,Silke UNOPS Capacity Statement_Clean water and sanitation.pdf UNOPS_Capacity_Statement_Education.pdf UNOPS Capacity Statement_project_management.pdf\n\n\n\n \n\nOn Wed, Dec 11, 2024 at 8:59 PM\nAsbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\n\nDear Pia\n\n \n\nThank you very much for your flexibility. \n\n \n\nSilke Handley, Naimo Hirsi and myself will come to the\nFinnish embassy tomorrow at 11.00. \n\n \n\nSee you tomorrow! \n\n \n\nAll the best,\n\nAsbjørn\n\n \n\nOn Wed, 11 Dec 2024 at 20.52, Korpinen Pia (UE) <pia.korpinen@gov.fi>\nwrote:\n\nYes, I can manage 11-12.\n\nPlease let me know how many persons you will be so I can inform the guards.\n\n\n\nGood night and see you tomorrow,\n\nPia\n\n\n\n11.12.2024 17.09 Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> kirjoitti:\n\nDear Pia\n\n\n\nUnfortunately 2-3 pm clashes a bit with another commitment I have.\n\n\n\nWould it be possible to meet earlier? For example at 11-12?\n\n\n\nBest\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\nOn Wed, 11 Dec 2024 at 12.26, Korpinen Pia (UE) <pia.korpinen@gov.fi<mailto:pia.korpinen@gov.fi>>\nwrote:\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nVery sorry! I thought I had responded but clearly not, apologies our schedules\nare very busy.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI had booked for 2-3pm tomorrow, hope it works for you?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBest wishes,\n\n\n\nPia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org<mailto:asbjornb@unops.org>>\n\nSent: keskiviikko 11. joulukuuta 2024 10.40\n\nTo: Korpinen Pia (UE) <pia.korpinen@gov.fi<mailto:pia.korpinen@gov.fi>>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org<mailto:naimoh@unops.org>>;\nSilke Grundmann HANDLEY <silkeh@unops.org<mailto:silkeh@unops.org>>\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS and Finland in Ethiopia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Pia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCould I kindly ask if you have had a chance to see when you might be available\nto meet tomorrow?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you in advance.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBest,\n\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Mon, 9 Dec 2024 at 12.09, Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org<mailto:asbjornb@unops.org>>\nwrote:\n\n\n\nDear Pia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you very much for your rapid response.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI’m available Thursday afternoon at your convenience. I’ll wait for you to get\nback to me regarding the specific time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you in advance.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBest\n\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Mon, 9 Dec 2024 at 11.59, Korpinen Pia (UE) <pia.korpinen@gov.fi<mailto:pia.korpinen@gov.fi>>\nwrote:\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for your message and thank you for reaching out. I could manage a\nmeeting on Thursday afternoon, but unfortunately our Head of Cooperation, who\nwould be most relevant for you to meet, is out of country end of this week. I\nwill in any case check with my other colleagues if anyone else would be\navailable, and will let you know asap. This just to flag that Thu afternoon\nwould be the available time-slot and will still get back to you later today to\nconfirm.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org<mailto:asbjornb@unops.org>>\n\nSent: maanantai 9. joulukuuta 2024 11.17\n\nTo: Korpinen Pia (UE) <pia.korpinen@gov.fi<mailto:pia.korpinen@gov.fi>>\n\nCc: Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org<mailto:naimoh@unops.org>>;\nSilke Grundmann HANDLEY <silkeh@unops.org<mailto:silkeh@unops.org>>\n\nSubject: UNOPS and Finland in Ethiopia\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Pia,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMy name is Asbjørn Brink, and I am heading the Northern Europe Liaison Office\nwithin UNOPS, headquartered in Copenhagen.\n\n\n\nI am writing as I will be in Addis on December 12-13 and would greatly\nappreciate the opportunity to meet with you and your relevant colleagues along\nwith my local UNOPS colleagues in Addis (cc this email).\n\n\n\nDuring our meeting, I would be delighted to explore how UNOPS could further\ncontribute to advancing Finland's development aid priorities. Our expertise in\nproject implementation, infrastructure, procurement, and capacity building\npositions us as a strong partner in achieving shared objectives, particularly\nin areas such as climate resilience, gender equality, and inclusive economic\ndevelopment.\n\n\n\nWe would also like to share some recent examples of UNOPS’ impactful work\nacross the African continent. From building climate-resilient infrastructure in\nvulnerable regions to enhancing access to healthcare and education in\nunderserved communities, our initiatives align closely with Finland's focus on\npoverty reduction and sustainable development.\n\n\n\nI would greatly appreciate it if you could please let me know if you are\navailable for a meeting on December 12 or 13. We look forward to the\nopportunity to discuss potential synergies and ways we can collaborate to\namplify Finland's development goals.\n\n\n\nThank you very much in advance for your time and consideration.\n\n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAsbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and\nLiaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org<https://www.unops.org/english/Pages/Home.aspx>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKeep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook<https://www.facebook.com/unops.org/>,\nLinkedIn<https://www.linkedin.com/company/unops>,\nTwitter<https://twitter.com/unops>,\nInstagram<https://www.instagram.com/unops_official/?hl=sv>,\nYouTube<https://www.youtube.com/user/UNOPSofficial>\n\n\n\nSubscribe to our external newsletter in English<https://mailchi.mp/8987deaa0e61/uojskr902j>,\nFrench<https://mailchi.mp/unops.org/gu0ld93is9>\nor Spanish<https://mailchi.mp/edf4b84d88cf/on3qnjwzkh>.\n\n\n\n[https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/nPxpbWSDHa0CL7JyQZX-4y85Mxn4y5gEFRdjC7t_CF_ptBC0_9XBSY2ZptDg9-nyWZQzuWxNqh-iqm0hCjymAwDk6KVXl7CvNjzi3PTAkCxhXNXzCWRmkUFCpULjbizB2mni1nMhp9Bzvs4_VZ_uU2I]",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000LNkPXMA1",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "pia.korpinen@gov.fi", "silkeh@unops.org", "workneshg@unops.org", "naimoh@unops.org", "asbjornb@unops.org" },
