                    "00TQx00000L1MdmMAF",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Fwd: Your application for Sida's humanitarian partnership",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-31").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Fwd: Your application for Sida's humanitarian partnership",
                        Description = "To: Katarina.Zinn@sida.se\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Fwd: Your application for Sida's humanitarian partnership\nBody:\nDear Katarina,\nI hope this email finds you well on the verge to a well-deserved weekend. \nI am reaching out to you, as we at UNOPS have been applying to become a trusted partner of SIDA on humanitarian aid. Unfortunately our application has been rejected (cf. message below) - apparently because UNOPS does not fulfill one or more of the eligibility criteria. This is a bit of a surprise to me - and I would appreciate if you could help look into which specific criteria UNOPS does not fulfill. \nThank you very much in advance for looking into this matter. \nWishing you a wonderful weekend! \nAll the best,Asbjørn\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Humpartnership <humpartnership@sida.se>\nDate: Thu, 30 Jan 2025 at 16:18\nSubject: Your application for Sida's humanitarian partnership\nTo: \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear applicant,\n \nWe want to thank you for your application to the\nCall for expression of interest for humanitarian partnership with Sida. A total of 105 applications were received, which were then appraised against the eligibility criteria.\nMany of the applications were of high quality which made the process highly competitive.\n \nBased on the information provided in your application, Sida assesses that your organization does not meet one or more of the eligibility criteria* for this\n partnership modality. Your organisation will therefore not proceed to the next step of the assessment process. For more information on the assessment method kindly see the FAQ that will be published on\nwww.sida.se\n in the coming days.\n \n\nOver the next strategy period, Sida envisages having several partnership modalities. This call for expression of interest relates to one of these modalities: core operational partnerships\n with organisations delivering humanitarian assistance and protection. The fact that your organisation was not successful in this particular process does not exclude future partnership with Sida. Sida may launch additional calls for partnerships in due course,\n to ensure effective implementation of the next humanitarian strategy.\n \nWe encourage you to monitor Sida’s website for information and updates regarding future calls or processes for humanitarian partnership with Sida.\n \nOnce again, thank you for your interest in partnering with Sida.\n \nKind regards,\n \nBilan\n \nBilan Osman Jama\nDeputy Humanitarian Director,\nHumanitarian Department, Sida\n\n\n\n\nSwedish International Development Cooperation Agency (Sida)\n\n\nWeb:\nsida.se\n| openaid.se\n\n\n\n\n\nPostal address: Box 2025, SE-174 02 Sundbyberg, Sweden\n\n\nProcessing of personal data\n\n\n\n\n\nVisiting address: Rissneleden 110, Sundbyberg\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n*Eligibility criteria were set out in the questionnaire that you used to submit the application.\n\n\n\n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
