                new (
                    "00TQx00000KZiqvMAD",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Catch-up: Finland/UNOPS",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-21").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Catch-up: Finland/UNOPS",
                        Description = "To: Mervi.Kultamaa@gov.fi; Sanna.Luomanpera@gov.fi\nCC: naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Catch-up: Finland/UNOPS\nBody:\nDear Mervi and Sanna\nI look forward to our introduction talk as soon as you are available to meet online. As mentioned in our separate email exchanges, unfortunately I won't be going to New York for the upcoming Executive Board this time. But I hope that we get to catch up online soon. \nIn advance of our intro call, I wanted to flag that it would be good if we could initiate a dialogue on updating the current standard template for engagements between UNOPS and Finland. We have recently signed an engagement with your colleagues in Nepal to support the creation of a gender-inclusive framework for Nepal’s National Urban Development Strategy. During this conversation your colleagues realised that the current template was outdated. Due to a very tight time schedule for signing the engagement, we agreed to work on updating the global standard template - and then potentially amend the engagement in Nepal with any changes that may from from the global standard template. \nI would therefore be happy if you could help us initiate this dialogue on an updated standard template for engagements between UNOPS and Finland. I assume that from your end it would be your legal team (which would be the same here)? \nIn case you have already recently agreed on such standard template with other similar UN agencies, it would be super helpful for us if you could kindly share this with us - and perhaps use that as a starting point for the conversation. \nPS - your colleagues in Kathmandu might also reach out to you / your colleagues in your legal team to initiate this dialogue on a new standard template. Just flagging this to avoid any confusion. \nLooking very much forward to hearing back from you. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
