                new (
                    "00TQx00000KMoQsMAL",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: RE: Review of Arkas",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-15").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: RE: Review of Arkas",
                        Description = "To: asbjornb@unops.org\nCC: massimodi@unops.org; teresam@unops.org; eleneag@unops.org; arunn@unops.org; svitlanas@unops.org; svitlanaz@unops.org; annkah@um.dk\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: Review of Arkas\nBody:\nDear Asbjørn\n \nThank you very much for gathering the requested information. This is most helpful and will enable the review team to come up with findings\n that I’m sure will benefit us all as we agree on the onwards process. \n \nAs for your request to keep the material confidential, we will make this clear to the review team.\n\n \nThank you\nSune\n_______________________________________________________\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ /\nSUNGUD@UM.DK\nCHIEF ADVISOR\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n \nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n/\nWWW.UM.DK\nHOW\n WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION\n \n\nPlease\n consider the environment before printing this message\n \n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 15 January 2025 14:27\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>\n\nCc: Massimo DIANA <massimodi@unops.org>; Teresa MOLERO RODRIGUEZ <teresam@unops.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Svitlana Stadnyk <svitlanas@unops.org>; Svitlana ZAKRYNYTSKA <svitlanaz@unops.org>; Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>\n\nSubject: Re: Review of Arkas\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find attached the \nrequested documentation for your review. \n\n\n \n\n\nKindly notice that the documents contain eg. confidential contractual arrangements between UNOPS and third parties - for which we have had to acquire the approval of third parties to share the information. We therefore kindly ask for you\n to not share the documents beyond the reviewer and please treat the package as confidential in general. \n\n\n \n\n\nOur entire team remains at your disposal for any follow-up inquiries related to this review, and we would be more than happy to speak with the reviewer to explain the process of tenders, designs, assignments, etc.     \n\n\n \n\n\nWe look very much forward to hearing back from you. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n \n\n\nOn Mon, 9 Dec 2024 at 10:47, Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn\n \nAs briefly discussed a few weeks ago, we are proposing to have a review of the Arkas project to provide the City\n with a second opinion and quality assurance of the plans for undertaking the reconstruction of the building.\n\n \nIn order to proceed, it would be very helpful if UNOPS could kindly share the following documents from your initial\n study:\n \n\nAll tender-related documentation, including Terms of Reference, for the stabilisation of ArkasAll UNOPS’ contracts with all (sub-)contractors (advisory, construction, legal and so forth)All assignments, design project tasks and others presented by UNOPS to UNOPS’ (sub-)contractorsAll UNOPS’ contracts and other legal commitments with local stakeholders such as the Capital Construction Department\n of the Mykolaiv City AdministrationInitial designs and estimates for the full reconstruction of Arkas\n \nE-mail correspondence and similar communication between UNOPS, the contractor and local authorities may be required.\n The document are initially for DMFA’s internal use but we would like to know whether UNOPS has any reservations about these documents being released for external review by the contractor identified for this assignment.\n\n \nKind regards\nSune\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\n\n \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group\n | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
