                        Description = "To: Mervi.Kultamaa@gov.fi\nCC: naimoh@unops.org; Sanna.Luomanpera@gov.fi\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Documents for upcoming Executive Board 27-31 January\nBody:\nDear Mervi and Sanna\nMight Monday, January 20 any time after after 12.00 pm CET work for you? Or Tuesday. January 21 any time after 12.00 pm?\nbest,Asbjørn\nOn Wed, 15 Jan 2025 at 16:26, Kultamaa Mervi (UM) <Mervi.Kultamaa@gov.fi> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjorn,\n \nSorry for the delay in my response, we would be happy to meet you online, but would you have some other suggestions for\n the timing? I leave it to Sanna to co-ordinate. \n \nBest regards,\n \nMervi\n \n \nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: tiistai 14. tammikuuta 2025 10.48\n\nTo: Kultamaa Mervi (UM) <Mervi.Kultamaa@gov.fi>\n\nCc: naimoh@unops.org; Luomanperä Sanna (UM) <Sanna.Luomanpera@gov.fi>; Haukka Jenny (UM) <Jenny.Haukka@gov.fi>; Virtanen Antti (UE) <Antti.Virtanen@gov.fi>; Malaty Ramses (UM) <Ramses.Malaty@gov.fi>\n\nSubject: Re: FW: Documents for upcoming Executive Board 27-31 January\n \n\n\nDear Mervi,\n\n\n \n\n\nThank you very much for your response and information on Satu's appointment as ambassador to Mozambique - which I now recall that Satu had actually informed me about a while ago. \n\n\n \n\n\nI look very much forward to continuing the close and constructive collaboration with you and your team, that we have had with Satu, Andrea, Antti and other of your colleagues. \n\n\n \n\n\nUnfortunately I will not be in NYC for the Executive Board this time around, but I would be very happy to meet you and your relevant colleagues online for a brief introduction and dialogue about the topics to be discussed at the next Executive\n Board meeting. Might tomorrow afternoon or Thursday January 16 at any time work for you? \n\n\n \n\n\nThank you in advance. \n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 14 Jan 2025 at 09:33, Kultamaa Mervi (UM) <Mervi.Kultamaa@gov.fi> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjorn,\nLet me thank you for the email sent to Satu and Jenny, on the information and the initiative.\n Satu has been assigned as our Ambassador to Mozambique, and we are still waiting for her successor to step in. I am the team leader for UNOPS, among other triple executive board organizations, and Sanna Luomanperä is the relevant desk officer. I copy this\n also to Antti Virtanen in our mission and Deputy Director Ramses Malaty, with whom I will travel to New York for the triple executive board meeting. The outlined topics to be discussed is also a very useful overview for us.  We´ll study the issues and revert.\n A brief virtual meeting would we also welcome.\nBest regards,\nMervi\n \n\nMervi Kultamaa\n\nTeam Leader, UN Development Issues\n\nUnit for UN Development and Innovation Issues\n\n \n\nTel.\n +358 295 350 563\n\nMervi.Kultamaa@gov.fi\n\n\n\nMinistry for Foreign Affairs of Finland\n\nP.O. Box 176, Laivastokatu 22 A\n\nFI-00023 Government, Finland\n\n\n\num.fi\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n:\n\n\nLähettäjä: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nPäiväys: 13. tammikuuta 2025 klo 15.58.21 UTC+2\n\nVastaanottaja: \"Lassila Satu (UE)\" <Satu.Lassila@gov.fi>\n\nKopio: KEO-40 UM <KEO-40@gov.fi>, \"Haukka Jenny (UM)\" <Jenny.Haukka@gov.fi>, Naimo HASSAN HIRSI <naimoh@unops.org>\n\nAihe: Documents for upcoming Executive Board 27-31 January\n\n\n\n\n﻿\n\nTämä viesti on lähetetty vanhaan ministeriökohtaiseen (@formin.fi) sähköpostiosoitteeseen. Toimiasi tarvitaan: Katso tarkempi ohje Kampuksen uutisesta.\n\nVanhojen ministeriökohtaisten sähköpostiosoitteiden käyttö loppuu. Varsinainen sähköposti, jonka sait, on tämän tekstin alla. VN-postin tiedote päättyy tähän.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nDear Satu and colleagues in Helsinki, \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nA late - but very happy new year to all of you! I hope you have had a chance to enjoy some offline time with your loved ones. \n\n\n \n\n\nAs usual I wanted to provide you with a brief overview of the topics relevant for UNOPS at the upcoming EB session on January 27-31. I am sorry that I am a bit late with this overview,\n as we already have the first informal session this afternoon at 5 pm CET about the status of the Comprehensive Response Plan and UNOPS' digitalisation plan (the so-called PID). \n\n\n \n\n\nI am sure that you have already seen that all the relevant documents were uploaded to the website here -\n but I just wanted to share the link with you to gather all the pieces in one email. \n\n\n \n\n\nI was wondering if perhaps you would have time to briefly catch up in advance of the EB - to get your initial take on the topics and for me to perhaps clarify matters, point towards\n (for us) important aspects, etc. If so - please just let me know when it might suit you. \n\n\n \n\n\nFurther to the topics to be discussed at the upcoming EB, I have provided you with a quick overview of the upcoming informal session below for your ease of reference. \n\n\n\n\n·      \n13 January: The comprehensive response plan and the UNOPS report on the Process Innovation and Digitalization Programme implementation \n\n·      \n14 January: Informal consultation with UNDP, UNFPA, UNOPS on the joint update on organization culture \n\n·      \n17 January: Joint UNDP, UNFPA, UNOPS orientation for the Executive Board (our DED Sonja will give an introductory presentation on UNOPS to the EB members)\n\n·      \n20 January: Briefing on undisbursed excess reserves, with UNBOA \n\n·      \n21 January: Joint consultation on enterprise risk management \n\n·      \n22 January: Joint informal with JIU on JIU report on governance and oversight \n\n\n\nThere will also be two closed session during the EB week:\n\n\n\n·      \n28 January: Closed briefing on S3i funds recovery, with OLA\n\n·      \n30 January: Closed briefing on portfolio risk assessment\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\nTopics to be discussed at the EB relevant to UNOPS\n\n\n\n1.     UNOPS'\n response to the recommendations of the UN Board of Auditors for 2023 \n\n\no  \nThe UNBOA report for 2023 on UNOPS was unqualified (also known as \"clean\") - meaning that our financial statements are deemed to present a true and fair view of UNOPS' financial position and performance, comply with UN accounting standards and are free\n of material misstatements. \n\no  \nUNBOA issued 9 recommendations classified as high priority and 10 recommendations classified as medium priority.  The implementation of all recommendations is on track for completion within the timelines. Because the recommendations were issued in July\n 2024, and many of them require long-term attention, UNOPS will need to work beyond 2024 to implement them all successfully.\n\no  \nIn the implementation schedule UNOPS is targeting an implementation rate of 68% during the 2024 audit cycle, which will surpass that of 2023 (58%).\n\n2.     Governance and oversight functions of the Executive Board \n\n\no  \nAt the last EB session the Bureau was tasked to develop a terms\n of reference for the operationalisation of a working group to review the 31 recommendations of the Joint Inspection Unit (JIU) and to develop actions\n for their implementation. \n\no  \nIn advance of the last EB session in 2024, UNOPS developed this\n informal document outlining UNOPS' views on the JIU recommendations. The document also contains the views of the ethics offices of the involved agencies. \n\n3.     Risk management \n\no  \nAt the last EB session, UNDP, UNFPA and UNOPS were asked to provide updates on the agencies' efforts to improve the enterprise risk management system and inform the EB of any critical risks of strategic importance. \n\no  \nFrom a UNOPS perspective The\n joint information note points towards key risks associated with project delivery, financial management and stakeholder engagement. It also points to more concrete risks regarding UNOPS' operations in fragile and conflict affected places, shortage of talent,\n sexual abuse due to the geographical operations of UNOPS, regaining trust among partners since S3i failures, implementing the many reforms at UNOPS and increasing financial constraints.     \n\n4.     Organisational culture \n\no  \nThe informal information\n note provides an update on the implementation of the work plan to transform the organisational culture. Status of each action point is in this\n annex.    \n\n5.     Implementation\n of the Comprehensive Response Plan \n\no  \nThis is the last update to the EB on the implementation of the CRP. As the note was written in November, 3 of the outstanding recommendations were yet to be completed by the end of 2024. These related to 1) revising the management and organisational\n culture towards broader engagement and less top-down, 2) invest in outcome-reporting, and 3) revision of financial rules and regulations.  \n\no  \nThe EB is asked to release the third tranche (11.8M USD) for the implementation and to initiate the second independent review of the implementation of the CRP.  \n\n6.     Review\n of the whistleblower process \n\no  \nThe informal information note provides an overview of the now completed overhaul of UNOPS' whistleblower mechanism. \n\no  \nThe new system is set to launch in January 2025 and will introduce: 1) a central platform for reporting, 2) ressources to provide early informal guidance, 3) a workplace conduct team within PLG, 4) a new advisory group to address systemic issues. \n\n7.     Portfolio risk assessment of UNOPS\n\n\no  \nAs a response to the original KPMG recommendations a\n portfolio risk assessment is presented that outlines a number of risks in UNOPS' portfolio. These relate e.g. to 1) challenges in managing complex infrastructure projects, 2) large-scale procurement of health products, 3) capacity of supplivers and implementing\n partners. \n\n8.     Calculation\n method for excess reserves \n\no  \nThe note presents a suggestion for revising the calculation methodology for calculating UNOPS' excess reserves. The proposed changes are to ensure that only liquid assets are calculated as part of the potential excess reserves and that only if the excess\n reserve exceeds 20% of the minimum operational reserve, it should trigger the refund process. \n\no  \nBy the end of 2023 UNOPS distributed 123.2M USD of the excess reserve back to partners and all other funds had been transferred to the RC system and the SDG fund. Only 0.6M USD is withheld as these relate to discussions with partners. \n\n9.     Implementation\n of the PID \n\no  \nThis is the annual status of implementation of the PID that points towards progress in seven programmes (country engagements, partnerships and project management, procurement, HR, finance, data, market research for the new ERP). \n\no  \nNotice that the selection of a new ERP system can only be done after a formal evaluation is presented to the EB (as requested by the EB). Therefore the timeline for the PID has been extended by one year to 2028.\n\n\nI hope this brief overview helps - and I look very much forward to hearing your initial thinking about the topics. \n\n\n\n \n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\n \n\n--\n\n\n\n \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ\n | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nTämä viesti on osoitettu ainoastaan sen tarkoitetulle vastaanottajalle ja se saattaa sisältää salassa pidettävää tietoa. Jos et ole viestissä tarkoitettu vastaanottaja, tuhoa viesti ja ilmoita asiasta välittömästi viestin lähettäjälle.\n Viestin sisällön, välitystiedon ja viestin olemassaolon hyväksikäyttäminen ja ilmaiseminen on kielletty laissa (laki sähköisen viestinnän palveluista 136 § 4. mom).\n\n\n\n\nDetta meddelande gäller endast den avsedda mottagaren och kan innehålla sekretessbelagd information. Om du inte är den avsedda mottagaren ska du radera meddelandet och informera avsändaren omedelbart. Det är enligt lag förbjudet att utnyttja eller röja meddelandets\n innehåll, förmedlingsuppgifterna eller uppgifterna om meddelandets existens (136 § 4 mom. i lagen om tjänster inom elektronisk kommunikation).\n\n\n\n\nThis email message is intended only for the person(s) named in the message header and may contain privileged information. If you are not the intended recipient of this message, please delete the message and notify the sender immediately. Any disclosure or use\n of the content or traffic data of this message or the knowledge of its existence is prohibited by law (Act on Electronic Communications Services, section 136, subsection 4).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\n\n \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ\n | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-- \n\nAsbjørn Brink| Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Tel: +45 40 80 36 54 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
