                    "00TQx00000K8fCIMAZ",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Follow-up on proposal discussion",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-01-10").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Follow-up on proposal discussion",
                        Description = "To: aslnal@um.dk\nCC: claudiar@unops.org; asbjornb@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Follow-up on proposal discussion\nBody:\nDear Aslak, \nWishing you a happy 2025!\nIt was an absolute pleasure meeting you and once again thank you so much for welcoming me at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. \nI wanted to kindly follow-up on our recent discussion regarding the proposal focused on developing technical and financing models to maximize access to solar energy and energy-efficient cooling solutions in the date and dairy value chains across five areas in Tunisia. For reference, please find attached the proposal as well as an overview of UNOPS’ presence in North Africa. \nTo summarise, the proposal focuses on enhancing access to solar energy and energy-efficient cooling solutions in Tunisia's date and dairy value chains. It aims to develop technical and financing models that will benefit over 3,000 farmers, fostering sustainable livelihoods and addressing root causes for migration. Agriculture contributes 10% to Tunisia’s GDP and employs 16% of the workforce, with dates accounting for 12% of the total value of agricultural exports. The proposal is developed in collaboration with UNEP and incorporates a multi-donor funding model, making it easy for Denmark to take part in together with other partners. \nAs we discussed, there is much alignment between this project and the DAPP priorities; climate action, youth employment, and migration. \nIn the meeting, I also noted that Denmark could potentially be interested in supporting initiatives such as these projects carried out by UNOPS on behalf of our partners in Tunisia: Support to Tunisia's Border Control and Management of Migration Flows (Italy),  Support for Maritime Border Management (EU), and Procurement Service Project for land border control (Italy). Adding additional support to successful and well-established projects offers significant value for money for Denmark. \nMy colleagues Claudia, Asbjørn and I would very much appreciate a virtual meeting with your team and relevant colleagues at MIGSTAB in week 2 or 4 to explore these collaboration opportunities. Could you kindly let us know when this might work for you? \nBest regards,Naimo\n-- \nNaimo Hassan Hirsi | Partnerships Analyst | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Tel: +45 2683 4878 | Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
