                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000JIr1LMAT",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: UNOPS cooperation with Danish MFA 2025-2028",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-12-16").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: UNOPS cooperation with Danish MFA 2025-2028",
                        Description = "To: marysiaz@unops.org\nCC: valentynp@unops.org; eleneag@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org; davidnm@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: UNOPS cooperation with Danish MFA 2025-2028\nBody:\nHi Marysia, \nWhile I think it is ok that we try to make the case, I would not put my money on our chances for success. \nThe Danes have already provided mine clearance support to the RC Trust Fund in Ukraine and to UNDP. I would expect that they will continue to do it this way. \nNotice that the MFA has already decided that UNOPS should be a contributor to implement their goal number 8.2.2 on \"Reconstruction of social infrastructure, including educational facilities, shelters, hospitals, residential areas etc. to provide basic living conditions for citizens in Mykolaiv (Mykolaiv city and oblast)\".\nIf we are to push a bit for inclusion of our mine clearance capabilities, I would suggest doing so in connection with the reconstruction of infrastructure - pointing toward the need to clear mines and unexploded ordinances before being able to meaningfully rebuild infrastructure - and to improve living conditions for citizens.  \nI would also suggest that we point towards our capability to operate not only in Mykolaiv - but throughout all of Ukraine. I definitely think that you should flag our experience in mine clearance done in connection to infrastructure and the specific mine clearing projects done for the Dutch and the French (as I recall). \nGiven the current issues on the Arkas High School project, I am very concerned that the Danes are even considering our capability to do infrastructure reconstruction. I would therefore caution pushing too much on more of our capabilities - but make sure that at least they have confidence in our infrastructure capacities. \nIf the meeting with Erik is online, I would be happy to join if convenient. \nIn any case - it would be really good to make sure that all UNOPS participants have carefully studied the attached draft Danish programming programming for Ukraine. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\nMykolaiv (Mykolaiv city and oblast)On Mon, 16 Dec 2024 at 09:14, Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org> wrote:\nHi Asbjorn\nA quick point and question for you: \nWe are in a unique UN position where we have expertise in Infrastructure, Procurement AND Mine Action.\nIn order to make our projects more holistic, people-centred and impact driven, we would like to include all 3 areas of expertise in future projects with Denmark. Do you think this might be possible and well received?\nThanksMarysia\nOn Mon, 16 Dec 2024 at 10:07, Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Valentyn, \nI am terribly sorry for my way too slow response to this one! \nThis is good news! As you know, the Danish MFA is currently drafting their multi-annual country programming for their Ukraine support. They have asked a consultancy firm led by Mr. Erik Bryld to write this. \nIt is therefore positive that they have selected UNOPS to be among the key implementing partners for procurement and infrastructure. It would be super if you and Elene could help provide Erik with information on UNOPS' unique capacities in terms of procurement and infrastructure. \nDon't hesitate to let me know if you would like for me to be part of the meetings with Mr. Erik Bryld. I am available at your convenience. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\nOn Tue, 10 Dec 2024 at 10:36, Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org> wrote:\nDear Asbjorn,\nI've just received the message below. Do you know anything about this? Please, advise how to proceed.Thank you for your time and assistance.\nValentyn\n\n---------- Forwarded message ---------\nFrom: Erik Bryld <eb@tanacph.com>\nDate: Tue, Dec 10, 2024 at 10:25 AM\nSubject: UNOPS cooperation with Danish MFA 2025-2028\nTo: <valentynp@unops.org>\nCc: Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>, Erik Toft <erik@consultantsfordevelopment.dk>, Nadia Siegler-Lathrop <nsl@tanacph.com>\n\nDear Valentyn,  The Danish Ministry of Foreign Affairs has made a preliminary decision on partners for Ukraine for the period 2025-2028, and UNOPS will remain one of the key partners. We have been asked to assist the Ministry in this process. I am writing to give you a short overview of the process from here, explain the expected main outputs, and ask that you identify a focal point at UNOPS (if not you) we can work with to ensure we have the correct information and meet the MFA deadlines. We foresee that the support to UNOPS will be aligned with Denmark's existing bilateral engagement with UNOPS in Ukraine, but that the implementation should have an enhanced focus on aligning with Ukrainian systems, policies and procurement regulations as well as those of the EU to improve the accession process. Denmark has just released its draft Country Strategic Framework for Ukraine, which I have attached to this email. We foresee that UNOPS will be one of the contributors to the following goal described on p 37 pp: 8.2.2 Reconstruction of social infrastructure, including educational facilities, shelters,hospitals, residential areas etc. to provide basic living conditions for citizens inMykolaiv (Mykolaiv city and oblast)\nProcurement of reconstruction needs (projects and equipment) as prioritised by Mykolaiv City and Oblast. In terms of outputs, we need to produce an internal project document (see attached), which could rely on UNOPS’s similar document or we could use the same documentation. We need to have the contours of a first rough draft document ready by 15 January 2025. We will then come to Kyiv the last week of January with the MFA and discuss and agree on the remaining details, possibly through a half-day workshop.    I look forward to your response and would like to have an online call already this week, if feasible, to discuss the process. This is also in light of our relatively short timeframe for this task. All the best, - Erik \n\n\nErik Bryld Managing DirectorTana Copenhagen \nPalægade 3, 4th \nDK-1261 Copenhagen K \nDenmark \n\nT  +45 3536 1915\nM +45 2557 9797\neb@tanacph.com \nwww.tanacopenhagen.com\n\n\n-- \nValentyn Povroznyuk | Partnerships Senior Officer | UNOPS Ukraine Multi-Country Office | 2 Parkova Road/9B Hrushevskoho St, Kyiv, 01021, Ukraine | Tel.: +380 67 754 8669 | www.unops.org \n\n\n\n-- \nMarysia Zapasnik | Head of Programmes | UNOPS Multi Country Office | Ukraine | Tel:+380 502918548 | WA: +44 7908613745 | www.unops.org",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000JIr1LMAT",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "erik@consultantsfordevelopment.dk", "marysiaz@unops.org", "eb@tanacph.com", "davidnm@unops.org", "nsl@tanacph.com", "naimoh@unops.org", "valentynp@unops.org", "annkah@um.dk", "asbjornb@unops.org", "eleneag@unops.org" },
