                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000IVnC6MAL",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Potentiel Partnership UNOPS and HPF",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-11-25").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Potentiel Partnership UNOPS and HPF",
                        Description = "To: pkm@humanpractice.org\nCC: elenage@unops.org; sarahdg@unops.org; amyn@unops.org; fumiea@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Potentiel Partnership UNOPS and HPF\nBody:\nDear Pernille \nThank you very much for summarizing and for your feedback from your dialogue with the LEGO Foundation. \nI am looping in a few of my colleagues from Nairobi to make them aware of our initial talks. \nAs agreed, the next step on our end will be to link up our respective colleagues in Nairobi to start drafting a short of Terms of Reference for the division of labour, areas of responsibility, initial budget allocations and eventually a sort of concept note or similar that we are able to share externally. We will initiate this work next week, when we will meet with your Kenya Country Director. \nWe look very much forward to bringing this forward together. \nI'll revert back to you after we have met with your Nairobi based colleagues. \nAll the best, Asbjørn\nOn Mon, 25 Nov 2024 at 07:56, Pernille Kruse Madsen <pkm@humanpractice.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn,\n \nI hope this message finds you well. I wanted to thank you once again for our great conversation last week, and I’m sending you warm greetings from Nepal.\n \nI had a productive discussion with Sidsel, CEO of the LEGO Foundation. She plans for us to attend their board meeting either in March or May, with March being\n the more likely option, though this depends on whether Chairman Thomas is able to attend in person. Before then, Sidsel will coordinate with Thomas to determine the scale of the donation we should pursue—whether it will be for 5, 10, or 20 schools, which would\n amount to between 3 and 12 million USD.\n \nAs agreed, I’ve summarized the key points from our conversation below, which we can use as a foundation for our ongoing work together.\n \n---------oooOooo--------\n \nHPF is the program lead in relation to LEGO.\nWe will establish an overarching steering committee, where HPF, LEGO, and UNOPS will all be represented.\n \nUNOPS will be responsible for procurement related to construction and\n materials for libraries, etc.\nAdditionally, we will set up a\nTechnical Committee, where HPF and UNOPS will review construction costings, the process for selection of contractors, and UNOPS will help build the capacity of HPF and the local community.\n \n---------oooOooo--------\n \nThe next step is for you, Asbjørn, and the UNOPS team to meet with the HPF Kenya Country Director in Nairobi at the start of December to discuss the local collaboration\n in more detail.\n \nI will keep you informed about developments with LEGO, and we will after your Kenya trip discuss collaboration documents and costs.\n😊\n \nPlease do let me know if I’ve missed anything, or if there is anything we should clarify further at this stage.\n \nI look forward to hearing how your discussions in Kenya are progressing.\n \nBest wishes,\n\n\n\n\nPernille\nPernille Kruse Madsen\nManaging Director \n |  Human Practice Foundation\n\nBrolæggerstræde 2, 1211 København K, Denmark\n\nCell: +45 61 51 73 00 \n |  Office: +45 93 93\n 27 74 \n\nMail: pkm@humanpractice.org\n \n\nWebsite: www.humanpractice.org\n\nFacebook: www.facebook.com/humanpracticefund",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000IVnC6MAL",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "elenage@unops.org", "amyn@unops.org", "sarahdg@unops.org", "naimoh@unops.org", "fumiea@unops.org", "pkm@humanpractice.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
