                    },
                    new List<string> { "003Qx00000T8OKbIAN" },
                    new List<int> {  },
                    new List<string> { "asbjornb@unops.org" },
                    new List<string> { "B0047" }
                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000HzS45MAF",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Project 24129.",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-11-12").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Project 24129.",
                        Description = "To: jakhas@um.dk\nCC: teresam@unops.org; svitlanaz@unops.org; arunn@unops.org; simonp@unops.org; marysiaz@unops.org; sungud@um.dk; annkah@um.dk; torlar@um.dk; artvas@um.dk; vaszal@um.dk\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Project 24129.\nBody:\nDear Jakob\nThank you for your response and valuable considerations on the way forward. \nWe are consulting a wider group of our legal experts and will provide additional written elaborated explanations in Ukrainian on the 4 remaining disagreements in the draft legal agreement with CCD (as an agreement with the contractor has been reached). Based on that, Teressa and Svitlana will meet with the CCD again on Tuesday next week to make another attempt to reach an agreement. Following this meeting we will consult with you again on the way forward. \nWe are very conscious of the fact that the CCD by the end of the day will be the formal recipient of the final reconstructed Arkas High School - and therefore has to be closely involved in the entire process, taking into account all of their input, technical advice, requests, etc. It is therefore crucial for the success of the reconstruction project that all parties (Denmark as the donor, UNOPS as the project manager, the contractor(s) and the CCD as the final recipient) are aligned. To ensure this we have for example incorporated legally binding requirements of monthly CCD inspections of the work. \nWe are flagging the issues on contractual disagreements to you now, as the negotiations with the contractor and the CCD have been ongoing for a long time with more than 20 iterations at working level with the CCD alone. If Teressa and Svitlana are not able to reach a workable solution with the CCD next week at their level, I believe that we need to escalate the matter. Otherwise I fear that too much time will be lost without substantive progress. \nWe may therefore need to call upon your help to escalate the matter with the local Ukrainian authorities to ensure that an amicable solution is reached with an agreement without potential conflicts of interests and a minimized risk assessment. \nAs outlined in Teressa's document (attached here for ease of reference), the contractor was selected after a public tender process approved by CCD. The contractor has requested that all communication between the contractor and CCD happens via UNOPS as the project manager - which would ensure arms length and avoid potential conflicts of interests, etc. \nTo specify the outstanding points, I have reiterated them below: CCD requests that UNOPS can only pay the contractor upon approval from CCDwould be a violation of UN financial rules and regulationsUNOPS would in practice lose control over the projectwould severely increase financial risk assessment\n\nCCF requests the right to terminate the agreement with the contractor unilaterally with a notice period of 30 daysunacceptable to contractorcould create unfortunate conflicts of interests between contractor and CCDin violation with UN financial rules and regulations as UNOPS is the entity contracting UNOPS would in practice lose control over the project\n\nCCD is to be the technical author and supervisorwhile CCD certainly should provide technical advice, requests, input, observations and must be consulted regularly (see agreement on monthly basis), the technical supervision of the reconstruction project has to be done by UNOPS as the project manager and as the responsible entity for ensuring the quality of the final product\n\nContractor has to eliminate defects after the first 12 months of finalising the projectthe defects notification period that can be accepted by UNOPS is 12 months which is standard for these types of infrastructure reconstruction projectsduring the first 12 months after finalising the reconstruction, flaws, etc. can be notified to UNOPS and we will make sure that it is dealt with within the 12 months period. For this reason we will only make the final payments to the contractor(s) after the 12 months defects notification period. We would be very happy to jump on a call at your convenience to elaborate on the matter. Otherwise I would suggest that we touch base during next week. \nWe remain as always at your entire disposal for any comments, questions, requests or otherwise. \nAll the best,Asbjørn\n\nOn Mon, 11 Nov 2024 at 13:21, Jakob Torrild Hansen <jakhas@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Teresa\n\n\n\nThank again for this comprehensive update. We have discussed this internally and have decided that before intervening as donor, we would like to first see from your side some suggestions on how this conflict could possibly be resolved – i. e. through a revised\n contract or other. An agreement between UNOPS, the CCD and UNOPS’ chosen contractor has to be reached in one way or another, and we find that UNOPS - with your available legal expertise as project manager - is in a better place to develop all options. We stand\n ready to review these as soon as you present them to us. \n \nBest regards,\nJakob\n \n\n\nFrom: Jakob Torrild Hansen\n\n\nSent: 11 November 2024 12:42\n\nTo: 'Teresa MOLERO RODRIGUEZ' <teresam@unops.org>\n\nCc: Svitlana ZAKRYNYTSKA <svitlanaz@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>; Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>;\n Torben Traustedt Larsen <torlar@um.dk>; Artem Vasalatii <artvas@um.dk>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>\n\nSubject: RE: Project 24129.\n\n\n \nDear Teresa\n\n\n\nThank you for this summary. I copy my colleagues, we will discuss internally and then revert to you.\n\n \nBest regards,\nJakob Torrild Hansen\n \nJAKOB TORRILD HANSEN /\nJAKHAS@UM.DK\nHEAD OF DANISH EMBASSY OFFICE IN MYKOLAIV\nTEL: +38 096 301 4072 (WHATSAPP, SIGNAL)\n \nROYAL DANISH EMBASSY – MYKOLAIV OFFICE\nLYAHINA 4/54001 MYKOLAIV, UKRAINE\n \n\n \n\n\nFrom: Teresa MOLERO RODRIGUEZ <teresam@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 11 November 2024 12:25\n\nTo: Jakob Torrild Hansen <jakhas@um.dk>\n\nCc: Svitlana ZAKRYNYTSKA <svitlanaz@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>;\n Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Project 24129.\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply,\n click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Jakob,  \n\n\n\nI hope this message finds you well.  \n\n\n\nAttached, you will find a summary of the agreement process necessary for applying for the permits for Arkas. This process commenced in July; however, it has not yet reached a final conclusion.\n\n\n\n\nWe would greatly appreciate the opportunity to arrange a meeting at your convenience to address any observations and, if needed, discuss the next steps forward.\n\n\nThank you\n\n\nBest\n\n\nTeresa\n\n\n \n\n-- \n\n\n\nTeresa Molero Rodríguez (Ella/She/her) | \n Project Manager |  Mykolaiv Infrastructure Project | UNOPS Ukraine Multi-Country Office |  Mykolaiv, Ukraine | Tel:  +34618939839 7 +380669645309 \n  | www.unops.org",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000HzS45MAF",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "simonp@unops.org", "arunn@unops.org", "marysiaz@unops.org", "vaszal@um.dk", "torlar@um.dk", "jakhas@um.dk", "artvas@um.dk", "svitlanaz@unops.org", "annkah@um.dk", "sungud@um.dk", "teresam@unops.org", "asbjornb@unops.org" },
