                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2024-10-23").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Draft concept note for \"Helsingør Dialogue\" - translating commitment into solutions on the ground",
                        Description = "To: marweg@um.dk; lotmac@um.dk; julwin@um.dk; tuewes@um.dk; rikoln@um.dk\nCC: emiliep@unops.org; rahulm@unops.org; naimoh@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Draft concept note for \"Helsingør Dialogue\" - translating commitment into solutions on the ground\nBody:\nDear Lotte, Marie-Louise and colleagues \nThank you for the pleasant meeting on Monday regarding the upcoming CEB as well as our idea of a \"Helsingør Dialogue\" focusing on the implementation bottlenecks. \nAs promised please find attached a digital version of our draft concept note for the Helsingør Dialogue for your review. \nWhile we will continue with the planning of the event in conversations with the SG, DSG and other relevant UN stakeholders, I hope that you would consider Jorge's offer to co-host the event. We believe that the focus on translating big promises into reality on the ground is very much in line with the solution oriented Danish approach and political agenda. \nA joint event could further help increase awareness of the strong UN presence in Copenhagen - and the focus in this specific event would underpin the Danish priorities of showcasing more clearly what the UN can deliver in terms of tangible results. \nMy colleagues Emilie and Rahul (both cc) are leading the taskforce that are planning the Helsingør Dialogue. We are all at your disposal for any comments, questions, clarifications, etc. \nI look very much forward to hearing back from you. \nBest regards,Asbjørn  Asbjørn Brink | Head of Northern Europe Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | UNOPS HQ | Copenhagen, Denmark | Mob: +45 40 80 36 54 | www.unops.org Keep up-to-date with UNOPS. Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube Subscribe to our external newsletter in English, French or Spanish.",
