                        Subject = "Email: ATACH membership",
                        Description = "To: villalobose@who.int\nCC: maierom@who.int; vincis@who.int; egorovaa@who.int; umbertov@unops.org; helen.yaxley@fcdo.gov.uk; elenali@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: ATACH membership\nBody:\nDear Elena and team\nThanks for organising the well chaired and interesting ATACH call this morning - and congratulations on the \"revitalisation\" of the structure and ways of working! \nHaving contributed to the various working groups, meetings and joint events at WHA, COP etc over the last couple of years, can you please kindly confirm whether UNOPS is already an \"official\" Partner in ATACH (I don't see us listed here). If not, please advise what the process is for becoming an official partner (fyi a WHO/UNOPS MoU was signed in 2015).\nAdvancing Climate Action is a priority at UNOPS and we continue to support WHO and member states with implementation capacity, to scale up Climate and Health initiatives, across solarisation for health care (Côte d'Ivoire, Somalia, Yemen, Haiti etc), climate resilient infrastructure, sustainable procurement, and more,  particularly in fragile and conflict affected settings. \nATACH is a well recognised platform to share the increasing body of evidence and data, experience and lessons learned which UNOPS is keen to contribute to, e.g. as was requested in today's call, guidance for engaging with private sector for energy / mini grid solutions; we have taken lessons from our rural renewable energy project in Sierra  Leone with FCDO and other partners - which are now being replicated in the Sahel  \nBeyond project implementation, we are also co-hosting the Santiago Network agreed at COP28, hosting SE for All and most recently working with the US to expand the Global Climate Action Partnership - ATACH is a great way to share this information, lessons and technical support, enabling more member states to benefit, and helping improve coordination. Please help us share! \nLooking forward to hearing from you on this issue, and continuing our collaboration with Maria, Marina and Alex on our upcoming COP29 panel on the WHO Pavilion.\nWith thanks and best wishes, Louise \n\nLouise Leech, MPH  | Head of Geneva Liaison Office | Partnerships and Liaison Group | Mobile: +41 79 343 1614  UNOPS / Office des Nations Unies pour les Services Unité de Gestion du Projet\nGlobal project overview here  |  Follow us on Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Instagram, YouTube",
