                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-04-04").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Follow-up: Energy/Heating Needs Project in Ukraine",
                        Description = "To: eleneag@unops.org; pablo.gan@aecid.es\nCC: marysiaz@unops.org; valentynp@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Follow-up: Energy/Heating Needs Project in Ukraine\nBody:\nDear Elene,\n\n\n\nThank you for your mail and for hosting us this week in your premises.\n\n\n\nAnd thank you indeed for this thorough information you share with us in your email.\n\n\n\nHave a nice weekend and receive our warm wishes,\n\n\n\nPatricio  \n\n\n\n\n\n\nPatricio Rumeu Casares\n\nConsejero/Counselor\n\nEmbajada de España en Ucrania / Embassy of Spain to Ukraine\n\nKhoryva 46 - 04071 Kyiv\n\n+ 38 044 5210732\n\ne-mail: patricio.rumeu@maec.es\n\n \n\n\n\nwww.exteriores.gob.es    \n         \n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\nSent: Friday, April 4, 2025 4:24:51 PM\n\nTo: pablo.gan@aecid.es <pablo.gan@aecid.es>; Rumeu Casares, Patricio <patricio.rumeu@maec.es>\n\nCc: Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Follow-up: Energy/Heating Needs Project in Ukraine\n \n\n\n\nDear Ambassador Quesada, Dear Patricio,\n\n\n\n\nFollowing up on our conversation, I wanted to provide an update regarding the potential project\n to address energy/heating needs in Ukraine.\n\n\n\n\nAs requested, we've gathered updated information on the district heating sector's priorities\n and critical needs, as identified by WASH partners. Attached, you'll find overviews of the district heating needs in:\n\nIzium, Kharkiv oblastBalakliya, Kharkiv oblastChernihivShostkaPoltava\nWe also have information from authorities in the Vinnytsia region, primarily covering modular\n boiler houses, which we can provide if that location is preferred.\n\n\n\n\nBased on this information, we would like to discuss your preferred location for the project.\n We suggest focusing on the procurement of:\n\nCogeneration unitsModular boiler housesPumps, pipes, valves, and other supportive materials\nTo give you an idea of costs, a 250-260 kW cogeneration unit is estimated at around USD 350,000,\n while a 5 MW modular boiler house is around USD 800,000-850,000. Supportive materials would be lower in cost.\n\n\n\n\nWith your prioritization, we can design a procurement project with an estimated duration of\n 11 months. Of course, we will coordinate with other partners to avoid duplication.\n\n\n\n\nIf this approach is acceptable, we will prepare a detailed concept note/project proposal.\n For you reference, we have also made initial high-level budget estimations for a project under USD 2 million:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEngagement Budget Categories\n\nTotal in USD\n\n\n\n\n\nActivities/Procurement\n\n$1,400,000\n\n\n\nPersonnel\n\n$302,193\n\n\n\nNon-personnel\n\n$145,193\n\n\n\nUNOPS Fee\n\n$144,224\n\n\n\nTOTAL\n\n$1,991,611\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease let us know your thoughts and we'd be happy to discuss this in more detail on a call.\n\n\n\nWith thanks and kind regards\n\n\n\nElene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, Apr 1, 2025 at 4:30 PM Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\nDear Ambassador Quesada, Dear Patricio,\n\n\n\nMany thanks for the meeting earlier today and for your interest in exploring partnership with UNOPS to support emergency needs in Ukraine.\n\n\n\nLet me share with you some background materials about UNOPS procurement rules and our partnership with the EU.\n\n\n\nWe appreciate your interest in strengthening the water and energy systems and we will revert soon with some options.\n\n\n\nWe look very much forward to working with you and please don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions on UNOPS operations in Ukraine or in general.\n\n\n\nKind regards,\nElene \n\n\n\nElene Agladze\n|Partnerships Specialist | Ukraine Multi-Country Office | Kyiv, Ukraine | Tel: +380 956 00 1880 |\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org",
