                        Subject = "Email: RE: Signed agreement: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project",
                        Description = "To: vadyms@unops.org\nCC: tinlun@um.dk; marysiaz@unops.org; eleneag@unops.org; asbjornb@unops.org; yevheniiaz@unops.org; vladyslavk@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: RE: Signed agreement: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\nBody:\nDear Vadym\n \nMany thanks\nSune\n_______________________________________________________\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ /\nSUNGUD@UM.DK\nCHIEF ADVISOR\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n \nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n/\nWWW.UM.DK\nHOW\n WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION\n \n\nPlease\n consider the environment before printing this message\n \n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Vadym SHCHEDRIN <vadyms@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 24 January 2025 09:42\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>\n\nCc: Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk>; Yevheniia ZHUK <yevheniiaz@unops.org>; Vladyslav Kyrii <vladyslavk@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Signed agreement: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\nDear Sune, \n\n \n\n\nI hope this email finds you well.\n\n\n \n\n\nPlease find the bank receipt attached.\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Jan 15, 2025 at 6:46 PM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Marysia\n \nI hope this finds you well. It seems that I have not received a bank receipt confirming the arrival\n if the funds in the UNOPS bank account. Could you kindly check whether this has been sent, acknowledging that with the holidays, the email may have slipped.\n\n \nThank you,\nSune\n \n\n\nFrom: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz\n\n\nSent: 17 December 2024 22:51\n\nTo: 'Marysia ZAPASNIK' <marysiaz@unops.org>; Vadym SHCHEDRIN <vadyms@unops.org>\n\nCc: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk>;\n Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>; Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Serhii Oleksandrovich\n Babkin <serbab@um.dk>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>;\n Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk>; Vladyslav Kyrii <VladyslavK@unops.org>;\n Jakob Torrild Hansen <jakhas@um.dk>\n\nSubject: RE: Signed agreement: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \nDear Marysia\n \nWe have processed the disbursement today so you should receive the funds shortly. Please send the verified\n bank statement upon receipt. \n \nFurther to earlier correspondence with Elene on 5 December, please adjust your budget to the amount\n of DKK 25,000,000.00 that has been agreed and allocated to the project. The disbursement request we received from UNOPS was for DKK 25,826,783.24.\n \nBest regards,\nSune\n\n_______________________________________________________\n\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ /\nSUNGUD@UM.DK\n\nCHIEF ADVISOR\n\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\n\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n\n \n\nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\n\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n\n/\nWWW.UM.DK\n\nHOW\n WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION\n\n \n\n\n\nPlease\n consider the environment before printing this message\n\n \n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 12 December 2024 13:45\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>; Vadym SHCHEDRIN <vadyms@unops.org>\n\nCc: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk>;\n Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>; Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Serhii Oleksandrovich\n Babkin <serbab@um.dk>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>;\n Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk>; Vladyslav Kyrii <VladyslavK@unops.org>;\n Jakob Torrild Hansen <jakhas@um.dk>\n\nSubject: Re: Signed agreement: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\nDear Sune\n\n\n \n\n\nGreetings and happy Thursday\n\n\nPlease find attached the signed Disbursement Request.\n\n\n \n\n\nThree quick points from our end:\n\n\n\n\nWe'd like to introduce you to Vadym Shchedrin (in cc) who is the Project Manager from the UNOPS side. Vadym will be based in Mykolaiv for the duration of the project.\nWe'd like to ask you who is the contact person from the Denmark side for this project?\nAnd finally, we'd like to ask if we could organize a kick-off meeting in Mykolaiv next Friday with relevant parties?\n\nMany thanks and looking forward to working with all of you on this very worthwhile and much needed project\n\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards\n\n\nMarysia\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, 11 Dec 2024 at 16:02, Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n \nGreat! Thank you. Standing by for the disbursement request.\n\n \nBest\nSune\n \n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 11 December 2024 14:55\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>\n\nCc: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk>;\n Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>;\n Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk>; Vladyslav Kyrii <VladyslavK@unops.org>;\n Jakob Torrild Hansen <jakhas@um.dk>\n\nSubject: Re: Signed agreement: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n \n\n\nThanks so much for this!\n\n\n \n\n\nEnclosed please find the countersigned agreement from our side. \n\n\n \n\n\nI will let our PM and Finance Colleagues revert with regard to the Disbursement request.\n\n\n \n\n\nWith thanks and kind regards,\n\n\nElene\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\nOn Wed, Dec 11, 2024 at 11:57 AM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n \nPlease find attached the signed agreement, commitment letter and disbursement request form.\n\n \nI would be grateful if you could return the counter-signed agreement and the disbursement request as\n soon as possible so that we can get the funds out before everything shuts down for the holiday break.\n\n \nKind regards,\nSune\n\n_______________________________________________________\n\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ /\nSUNGUD@UM.DK\n\nCHIEF ADVISOR\n\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\n\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n\n \n\nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\n\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n\n/\nWWW.UM.DK\n\nHOW\n WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION\n\n \n\n\n\nPlease consider the environment before printing this message\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 06 December 2024 10:12\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>\n\nCc: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>; Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk>;\n Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>;\n Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk>; Vladyslav Kyrii <VladyslavK@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n \n\n\nMany thanks for this. \n\n\n \n\n\nJust a note to say, that any currency conversions in our system are done based on the UNORE rate which is fixed every 15  days. As of 1st of December 2024, the UNORE rate for DKK\n stands at 7.068 which in our project case amounts to USD 3,537,068. It would be very difficult for us to fix the amount in DKK and use a different rate. Therefore, maybe we can put in the agreement the exact USD amount you would be transferring to avoid any\n confusion? \n\n\n \n\n\nWe will of course adjust the budget accordingly, which will affect the costs for activities, since operational costs can not be decreased at this point.\n\n\n \n\n\nLet us know if this works for you.\n\n\n \n\n\nWith kind regards,\n\n\nElene\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Thu, Dec 5, 2024 at 7:47 PM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n \nI think we’re almost there……\n \nAs for your questions:\n \n\n\nI have put signing date as December 6. I will let you know tomorrow whether we make it or whether it is pushed to Monday.\n\nCity and Region have agreed to the list of facilities – it stays as is. Only a comment about updating some of the equipment which Novo has been informed of.\n\nAs for the budget in the proposal: Kindly note that the exchange rate for the US dollar as of today is 707,88 DKK to one USD. This is significantly higher than the exchange rate used for the budget\n in the proposal resulting in a budget increase. Unfortunately, we are not able to go beyond the commitment of DKK 25,000,000.00 irrespective of the exchange rate. As per today’s exchange rate, our commitment is equivalent to USD 3,531,672 instead of the USD\n 3,635,835 stated in the budget in the proposal. \n \nKind regards,\nSune\n \n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: 04 December 2024 10:14\n\nTo: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org>\n\nCc: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk>; Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org>; Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk>;\n Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>;\n Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk>\n\nSubject: Re: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n \n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified\n the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n \n\n\nReally great we're proceeding with the finalization. Just to confirm:\n\n\n\n\nCan we aim for December 5th as an effective date in the Agreement?\nWhether the scope of the project and the list of hospitals have been confirmed by the Mykolaiv authorities so that we can correct the list in the  proposal if needed.\n\nMany thanks and All Best,\n\n\n\nElene\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, Dec 3, 2024 at 9:07 PM Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\nThanks, Sune. \n\n\n \n\n\nElene will do the same on our end. \n\n\n \n\n\n/Asbjørn\n\n\n \n\n\nOn Tue, 3 Dec 2024 at 20.06, Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk> wrote:\n\n\nDear Asbjørn\n\n\n\nThank you very much. This is great news indeed. I’ll progress with finalising the agreement and readying it for signature.\n\n\n\nBest regards\n\nSune\n\n\n\nSune Hjelmervik Gudnitz\n\nChief Adviser\n\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs, Denmark\n\nMobile: +4523725319\n\nOn 3 December 2024 at 17.43.45 CET, Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune\n\n\n\nThank you for your pragmatic suggestions, which we have discussed at length internally with our audit and investigations team and with our legal group.\n\n\n\nBased on these conversations I am happy to report that we can accept your suggestion for paragraph 8 in its entirety. I have therefore included in the attached as proposed by you.\n\n\n\nI am also happy to be able to include your request for a timing requirement in paragraph 5 - provided that these are \"credible\" allegations. The first sentence of paragraph 5 in the attached therefore reads: \"UNOPS shall promptly notify the Funding Source of\n any credible allegations of Financial Irregularities subject to UNOPS’ respective applicable rules, policies, and procedures (...)\"\n\n\n\nI hope that this addresses your remaining concerns and requests for the agreement.\n\n\n\nAll the best,\n\nAsbjørn\n\n\n\nOn Fri, 29 Nov 2024 at 17:46, Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Asbjørn and Elene\n\n\n\nThank you for the reply and suggestions. Please see my reply below your text in bold.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regards, and have a good weekend,\n\n\n\nSune\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org<mailto:asbjornb@unops.org>>\n\nSent: 28 November 2024 10:36\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>>\n\nCc: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org<mailto:eleneag@unops.org>>; Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk<mailto:markup@um.dk>>;\n Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk<mailto:vaszal@um.dk>>; Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk<mailto:tinlun@um.dk>>;\n Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org<mailto:simonp@unops.org>>; Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk<mailto:serbab@um.dk>>;\n Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org<mailto:marysiaz@unops.org>>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org<mailto:valentynp@unops.org>>;\n Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org<mailto:arunn@unops.org>>; Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk<mailto:annkah@um.dk>>;\n Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk<mailto:larspr@um.dk>>\n\nSubject: Re: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for your review and always rapid responses.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn the attached we have accepted the non-substantial track changes for other paragraphs than 5 and 8 to make it easier to read.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWith regards to paragraph 5, we are concerned that using the term ‘promptly’ can be interpreted to mean an almost immediate notification, which in some cases may not be possible depending on a number of factors (eg. if the awareness came via whistleblowing\n process or via audit, time to look into its credibility, prioritisation of resources, etc.). We would therefore propose to remove the timing requirement and leave it as “UNOPS shall notify“.\n\n\n\n- Would that be acceptable?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThere is a need for an indication of timing, to avoid differences in opinion about what is acceptable. We have, including very recently, had unfortunate experiences where the lack of an agreed timeline led to reporting coming forward very  late. In other standard\n agreements with multilateral partners is the wording the following:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  *   The United Nations shall promptly notify the Ministry of any allegations of Financial Irregularities of which it has been informed or has otherwise become aware, provided, however, that (i) the allegations directly relate to the Project funded by the\n Contribution or\n\n  *   XX will advise the donor immediately of credible allegations of fraud or corruption involving the contribution and will inform the Donor when an investigation is launched by XX, always subject to XX regulations, rules and procedures.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWould it be possible to say: UNOPS will notify the Funding Source immediately when an internal investigation is launched subject to credible allegations of fraud or corruption involving the contribution.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWith regards to paragraph 8 our concern is that the agreement can be interpreted to mean that Denmark has the right to question the independent investigations or operations of our independent Investigations and Audit Group (IAIG), which we cannot agree to.\n In this respect we would like to make you aware of our operational directives regarding investigations (see attached OD.ED.2022.01). See especially section 6: Accountabilities of IAIG Personnel for further background as to IAIG’s role and accountability.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIt remains unclear to us why para 8 is suggested deleted – all the more so since it is established policy with the UN Secretariat. The assertion that the MFA can question an internal investigation is correct, but the wording does not specify the IAIG – perhaps\n it is the absence of IAIG in the text that poses the challenge to UNOPS as the involvement of the IAIG normally would suggest ‘appropriate action’?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe therefore reiterate the suggestion that para 8 remains as is.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWith UNOIOS, it would appear to us that Denmark already has some arrangements between your auditors and UNOIOS auditors to be able to agree to the language. With some donors, our IAIG has an established relationship with its counterpart on the donor’s side\n memorialized through an MoU or within a template agreement for example.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWhile we do not (yet) have any such MoU or template agreement between UNOPS and Denmark - I believe that it would be useful to aim for such an established relationship to be solidified in a potential upcoming MoU / template. However, given the timing of this\n engagement I do not think that it would be possible to finalise such an MoU / template in time. We will however commit to incorporate language on such a collaboration in an MoU / template - and we would also commit to amend any past engagements once such an\n MoU / template has been established between UNOPS and Denmark.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Would that be acceptable?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you in advance.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\nElene and Asbjørn\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Wed, 27 Nov 2024 at 15:46, Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMany thanks for taking the time to review. While the changes generally appear acceptable, please have a look at paras. 5 and 8 where we have concerns with the suggestions.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nSune\n\n\n\n_______________________________________________________\n\n\n\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ / SUNGUD@UM.DK<mailto:SUNGUD@UM.DK>\n\n\n\nCHIEF ADVISOR\n\n\n\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\n\n\n\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\n\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\n\n\n\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n\n\n\n/ WWW.UM.DK<http://WWW.UM.DK>\n\n\n\nHOW WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION<http://um.dk/en/about-us/organisation/contact-information/the-ministry-of-foreign-affairs-of-denmark-personal-data-policy>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org<mailto:eleneag@unops.org>>\n\nSent: 27 November 2024 13:58\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>>\n\nCc: Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk<mailto:markup@um.dk>>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk<mailto:vaszal@um.dk>>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk<mailto:tinlun@um.dk>>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org<mailto:simonp@unops.org>>;\n Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk<mailto:serbab@um.dk>>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org<mailto:marysiaz@unops.org>>;\n Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org<mailto:valentynp@unops.org>>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org<mailto:arunn@unops.org>>;\n Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk<mailto:annkah@um.dk>>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk<mailto:larspr@um.dk>>;\n Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org<mailto:asbjornb@unops.org>>\n\nSubject: Re: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI hope all is well.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFollowing up to last week's exchanges, I am sharing the draft agreement with the comments from HQ on para 11. You will see that our legal team suggests edits in the section to align the language with UNOPS key principles, instructions and internal policies\n on fraud and corruption (see some enclosed).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLet us know your thoughts and we discuss as needed.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you and all the best,\n\n\n\nElene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Fri, Nov 22, 2024 at 9:44 AM Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org<mailto:eleneag@unops.org>> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for this note - we will try to speed up to make sure we sign prior to the 1st of December.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn General Conditions: it is UNOPS' internal document and does not require approval from the Executive Board as such. But colleagues confirmed, that the change in the GC is related to the language on Interest only. In our case, the Interest clause is regulated\n by the Special Conditions separately, so the update should have no bearing on the arrangements.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI will revert back as soon as I get feedback on anti-corruption clauses.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nElene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Thu, Nov 21, 2024 at 6:06 PM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for moving quickly on this – fully understandable that HQ legal team has to review. I look forward to hearing back from you and hope that we can still be on track for a December 1 commencement.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks for sending the updated General Conditions. Have these been approved by the Exec Board, or internally in UNOPS only?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nSune\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org<mailto:eleneag@unops.org>>\n\nSent: 21 November 2024 16:44\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>>\n\nCc: Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk<mailto:markup@um.dk>>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk<mailto:vaszal@um.dk>>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk<mailto:tinlun@um.dk>>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org<mailto:simonp@unops.org>>;\n Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk<mailto:serbab@um.dk>>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org<mailto:marysiaz@unops.org>>;\n Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org<mailto:valentynp@unops.org>>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org<mailto:arunn@unops.org>>;\n Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk<mailto:annkah@um.dk>>; Lars Von Spreckelsen-Syberg <larspr@um.dk<mailto:larspr@um.dk>>\n\nSubject: Re: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for your support in moving the process ahead.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI forwarded suggested clauses on anti-corruption to our HQ legal team. While we don't expect any issues since the language was approved by the OLA, they noted that the text is new to them and asked for some time to review.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn another note, our legal team asked to update the General Conditions section, since minor changes have been recently introduced in UNOPS GC. We understand there are no major changes, except for more detailed language on Interest in para 2.5. So, I have included\n the updated General Conditions in the Agreement as PDF, since the link to the updated GC is not publicly available yet.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLet me know if you have any questions and happy to discuss as needed.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nElene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Thu, Nov 21, 2024 at 2:17 PM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you again for all the work drafting the agreement.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn view of the circumstances, including ongoing corruption cases with other partners, I have consulted with our Financial Department regarding the need to have included in the actual agreement a clause regarding anti-corruption. As it stands, anti-corruption\n is only referred to via the link under Annex II – General Conditions, which we find insufficient.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAs the Ministry has recently agreed with the UN Secretariat Office of Legal Affairs on standard anti-corruption language for all future agreements between the Ministry and the United Nations Secretariat, I have included this as Article 11 in the draft agreement.\n Please let me know if this is agreeable to UNOPS.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n\nSune\n\n\n\n_______________________________________________________\n\n\n\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ / SUNGUD@UM.DK<mailto:SUNGUD@UM.DK>\n\n\n\nCHIEF ADVISOR\n\n\n\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\n\n\n\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\n\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\n\n\n\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n\n\n\n/ WWW.UM.DK<http://WWW.UM.DK>\n\n\n\nHOW WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION<http://um.dk/en/about-us/organisation/contact-information/the-ministry-of-foreign-affairs-of-denmark-personal-data-policy>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[https://umbrella/organisation/Themes/UNITED_NATIONS_SECURITY_COUNCIL_AND_DENMARK/PublishingImages/Pages/Campaign-profile-and-Visual-identity/E-mail%20signature.png]\n\n\n\n[cid:ii_1938d5f36a55b16b22]Please consider the environment before printing this message\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org<mailto:eleneag@unops.org>>\n\nSent: 20 November 2024 15:23\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>>\n\nCc: Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk<mailto:markup@um.dk>>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk<mailto:vaszal@um.dk>>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk<mailto:tinlun@um.dk>>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org<mailto:simonp@unops.org>>;\n Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk<mailto:serbab@um.dk>>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org<mailto:marysiaz@unops.org>>;\n Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org<mailto:valentynp@unops.org>>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org<mailto:arunn@unops.org>>\n\nSubject: Re: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMany thanks for this swift feedback.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI accepted all changes, including on the disbursement of funds and added the text of the proposal (description of activities) into the annex of the agreement.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn the proposal we had a typo in the budget summary. The correct figure for the total direct cost amount is USD 3,482,267 vs 3,842,267 and the numbers should add up now - apologies for the confusion.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWith this, I think we should be ready to sign, but let us know how you would like to proceed.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMany thanks and kind regards,\n\n\n\nElene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Wed, Nov 20, 2024 at 1:32 PM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for this, and for finding a solution to the management fee question. This is really helpful.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAttached the two docs with some minor edits.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  *   For the agreement, we in fact prefer to pay the full sum of DKK 25,000,000 in one go – I have therefore changed the wording in the payment schedule. Please ensure that this is equally corrected elsewhere in the documents where there might be information\n to the contrary. I have filled in our contact information.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  *   As for the proposal, I have a question regarding the calculation of the budget at the end. Please have a look. I have resolved your my comments as it seems that you have answered.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you and kind regards,\n\n\n\nSune\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org<mailto:eleneag@unops.org>>\n\nSent: 19 November 2024 13:06\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>>\n\nCc: Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk<mailto:markup@um.dk>>; Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk<mailto:vaszal@um.dk>>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk<mailto:tinlun@um.dk>>; Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org<mailto:simonp@unops.org>>;\n Serhii Oleksandrovich Babkin <serbab@um.dk<mailto:serbab@um.dk>>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org<mailto:marysiaz@unops.org>>;\n Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org<mailto:valentynp@unops.org>>\n\nSubject: Re: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIndeed, we made sure to cover both projects and respective agreements under one engagement with the same overall scope to keep the initial fee, although we would normally create a new engagement with a new fee structure in such a case. The new draft of the\n agreement is enclosed for your review.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for your detailed read and comments on the proposal. I tried to address those and made a few comments in the draft, but do let me know if you still have questions/concerns. Once cleared, I will clean the text and change the annex in the draft agreement\n as well.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAll the best,\n\n\n\nElene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, Nov 19, 2024 at 11:40 AM Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>> wrote:\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI spoke with Asbjørn this morning and I was happy to hear that you have found a solution on the question about the management fee so that we can go ahead an create a new project. To this effect, I understand that you are drafting a new agreement.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI have just had a closer reading of the revised draft proposal and have attached herewith my comments. Grateful if you could seek to accommodate and also do a general check for typos.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI will finalize the project documentation on my end so that we can endeavour to have everything singed for a start on 1 Dec.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease do not hesitate to reach out if you have any questions.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBest regards,\n\n\n\nSune\n\n\n\n_______________________________________________________\n\n\n\nSUNE HJELMERVIK GUDNITZ / SUNGUD@UM.DK<mailto:SUNGUD@UM.DK>\n\n\n\nCHIEF ADVISOR\n\n\n\nEUROPEAN NEIGHBOURHOOD / UKRAINE RECONSTRUCTION\n\n\n\nDIRECT +4533920639\n\n\n\nMOBILE +4523725319\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS, DENMARK\n\n\n\nASIATISK PLADS 2 / DK-1448 COPENHAGEN K\n\n\n\n/ WWW.UM.DK<http://WWW.UM.DK>\n\n\n\nHOW WE PROCESS PERSONAL INFORMATION<http://um.dk/en/about-us/organisation/contact-information/the-ministry-of-foreign-affairs-of-denmark-personal-data-policy>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[https://umbrella/organisation/Themes/UNITED_NATIONS_SECURITY_COUNCIL_AND_DENMARK/PublishingImages/Pages/Campaign-profile-and-Visual-identity/E-mail%20signature.png]\n\n\n\n[X]Please consider the environment before printing this message\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org<mailto:eleneag@unops.org>>\n\nSent: 12 November 2024 13:28\n\nTo: Sune Hjelmervik Gudnitz <sungud@um.dk<mailto:sungud@um.dk>>\n\nCc: Anne Kahl <annkah@um.dk<mailto:annkah@um.dk>>; Asbjorn BRINK <asbjornb@unops.org<mailto:asbjornb@unops.org>>;\n Simon PORTER <simonp@unops.org<mailto:simonp@unops.org>>; Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org<mailto:valentynp@unops.org>>;\n Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org<mailto:arunn@unops.org>>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org<mailto:marysiaz@unops.org>>;\n Vasyl Zalishchuk <vaszal@um.dk<mailto:vaszal@um.dk>>; Mariia Kupris <markup@um.dk<mailto:markup@um.dk>>;\n Tine Lunn <tinlun@um.dk<mailto:tinlun@um.dk>>; Sahil Adnan <sahadn@um.dk<mailto:sahadn@um.dk>>\n\nSubject: Correction: UNOPS: Mykolaiv Health Project\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[CAUTION - EXTERNAL EMAIL] This email was sent from outside the MFA organisation. DO NOT reply, click on links, or open attachments unless you have verified the sender and know the content is safe.\n\n\n\nDear Sune,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWith apologies,...",
