                new (
                    "00TQx00000NR3bAMAT",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Follow up on the meeting regarding the potential cooperation",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-03-30").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Follow up on the meeting regarding the potential cooperation",
                        Description = "To: eleneag@unops.org\nCC: k.mikulova@eib.org; g.gajda@eib.org; k.dorfler@eib.org; valentynp@unops.org; marysiaz@unops.org; arunn@unops.org; massimodi@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Follow up on the meeting regarding the potential cooperation\nBody:\nCorporate Use\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Elene\n \nThank you very much for your time, fruitful discussion we had and the information you provided.\n \nAs we discussed, the EIB is currently considering number of options to ensure the provision of TA at the municipal level for the implementation of upcoming Programme on financing\n social and affordable housing in Ukraine. As agreed, we will continue further consultations with you to better understand the possibility for our potential engagement.  Please, see below the synopsis of TA tasks expected to be delivered at the municipal level:\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nTA teams to provide advisory support and monitoring at the municipal level\nto establish transparent and participatory mechanism of project implementation at all phases of project cycle, including:\n\n\ncapacity development and day-to-day support to Project Implementation Unit in municipalities,\nsupport to the technical documentation development, including preparation/monitoring of project design documentation, verification, authors supervision.\n\ntechnical design checking, with the specific attention to the “Build Back Better” and comprehensive EE solutions in the design and implementation,\nprocurement related capacity development (incl. procurement plan and tender documentation),\n\nsupport in identifying implementation issues (social, environmental, corruption, sanctions, etc.)\nsupport in organising regular technical working groups and track progress with identification of any bottlenecks in implementation with proactively proposing solutions of acceleration\n implementation and disbursement,\nsupport in oversight and monitoring of the quality of construction works, including:\n\n\n\ncollecting and providing an information to EIB, Ministry, Promoter and Final Beneficiaries detailed technical and financial information on individual housing projects (new construction),\n including maturity, timeline, project cost and sources of financing, technical parameters, land availability, environmental issues, social issues, tenders\nphysical control of implementation and progress in line with the initial plan/design, identification of social, environmental and procurement issues, including corruption.\n\n\n\nsocial management and stakeholder’s engagement,\ninstitutional development of municipally owned housing company\n\n \n\nAs we briefly discussed, we will suggest the additional meetings to explore the details of the expected TA services, in particular anti-corruption and sanctions checks, as well as other\n technical details, if it is fine with you.\n\n \n\nKind regards\n\n \n\nOksana.\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nFrom: Elene AGLADZE <eleneag@unops.org>\n\n\nSent: Friday 28 March 2025 14:37\n\nTo: REMIGA Oksana Victorovna <o.remiga@eib.org>\n\nCc: Valentyn POVROZNYUK <valentynp@unops.org>; Marysia ZAPASNIK <marysiaz@unops.org>; Arun NARAYANAN <arunn@unops.org>; Massimo DIANA <massimodi@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Thank you and contacts\n\n \n\n\n \nDear Oksana,\n \nThank you for the excellent meeting today. We truly appreciate the trust you place in UNOPS and are eager to partner with you in addressing the significant housing needs in Ukraine.\n \nAs promised, please find attached brief flyers outlining UNOPS' portfolio and ongoing projects in Ukraine. Not referred to here is the recently added World Bank-funded Health Enhancement\n And Lifesaving (HEAL) project, which is operational as of last week.  For context on our regional experience in social housing, you can review the EU-funded Social Housing and Active Inclusion (EU-SHAI) project implemented by UNOPS in Serbia here:\nhttps://social-housing.euzatebe.rs/en/\n \nI can indeed confirm that we have a robust legal framework in place to proceed with our partnership. The Master Agreement (attached, along with the Letter of Understanding) allows\n for direct grant agreements between UNOPS and EIB and covers both advisory services and technical assistance.\n \nPlease don't hesitate to reach out if you require any further information.\nWe look very much forward to working closely with you in the coming weeks and months.\n\n\n \n\n\nKind regards,\n\n\n \n\n\nElene\n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nElene Agladze\n|Partnerships Specialist | Ukraine Multi-Country Office | Kyiv, Ukraine | Tel: +380 956 00 1880 |\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nLes informations contenues dans ce message et/ou ses annexes sont \n\nreservees a l'attention et a l'utilisation de leur destinataire et peuvent etre \n\nconfidentielles. Si vous n'etes pas destinataire de ce message, vous etes \n\ninformes que vous l'avez recu par erreur et que toute utilisation en est \n\ninterdite. Dans ce cas, vous etes pries de le detruire et d'en informer la \n\nBanque Europeenne d'Investissement.\n\nThe information in this message and/or attachments is intended solely for \n\nthe attention and use of the named addressee and may be confidential. If \n\nyou are not the intended recipient, you are hereby notified that you have \n\nreceived this transmittal in error and that any use of it is prohibited. In \n\nsuch a case please delete this message and kindly notify the European \n\nInvestment Bank accordingly.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------",
                        Location = null,
