                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Advancing Dialogue in the Area of Procurement",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-06-18").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Advancing Dialogue in the Area of Procurement",
                        Description = "To: nadege.jnbaptiste@oecs.int\nCC: antoinel@unops.org; dcrm@oecs.int; nadine.felicien@oecs.int; franceen.tilakchand@oecs.int; vernil.ferdinand@oecs.int; beverly.stange@oecs.int; oscar.seaman@oecs.int\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Advancing Dialogue in the Area of Procurement\nBody:\nDear Nadege:\nThank you for following up with UNOPS on electronic procurement possibilities for the OECS general procurement. Kindly keep me informed on any significant developments.\nBest regardsFB\nOn Wed, 18 Jun 2025 at 11:46, Nadege Jn Baptiste <nadege.jnbaptiste@oecs.int> wrote:\nDear Antoine,\nI hope all is well and that your meeting with Chamberlain at the UNOC in France went very well and proved fruitful.\n\nI’m writing to follow up with great enthusiasm on our recent discussions and the agreed next steps relating to exploring procurement collaboration. In particular, I am keen to continue our dialogue on:\nKnowledge exchange on electronic procurement systemsInsights and cooperation around sustainable procurement practicesWe are indeed very interested in organising a dedicated session to explore the tools and systems used by UNOPS to manage highly complex procurement processes, especially in the Latin America and Caribbean region. This would be incredibly useful for informing our own processes and systems and how we can harness modern electronic technology to enhance cost efficiency and operational agility in line with broader efforts.\n\nI think it would therefore prove useful to schedule a follow-up meeting with our Procurement Unit to explore how we can advance collaboration in these areas.\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you and to building on this exciting opportunity.\nSincerely,\nNADEGE JN BAPTISTE (MS)HeadW: 758-455-6370   E: nadege.jnbaptiste@oecs.int\nOrganisation of Eastern Caribbean States (OECS) CommissionMorne Fortune, P.O.Box 179, Castries, Saint Lucia www.oecs.int | vCard |  Follow us on: facebook | twitter | youtube \n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis transmission (including any attachments) may contain confidential information, privileged material (including material protected by the solicitor-client or other applicable privileges), or constitute non-public information. Any use of this information by anyone other than the intended recipient is prohibited. If you have received this transmission in error, please immediately reply to the sender and delete this information from your system. Use, dissemination, distribution, or reproduction of this transmission by unintended recipients is not authorized and may be unlawful.\n-- \n\nSincerely,\nFRANCIS BURNETTInterim Head of Pooled Procurement ServicesW: 758-455-6355   E: francis.burnett@oecs.int\nOrganisation of Eastern Caribbean States (OECS) CommissionMorne Fortune, P.O.Box 179, Castries, Saint Lucia www.oecs.int | vCard |  Follow us on: facebook | twitter | youtube \n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis transmission (including any attachments) may contain confidential information, privileged material (including material protected by the solicitor-client or other applicable privileges), or constitute non-public information. Any use of this information by anyone other than the intended recipient is prohibited. If you have received this transmission in error, please immediately reply to the sender and delete this information from your system. Use, dissemination, distribution, or reproduction of this transmission by unintended recipients is not authorized and may be unlawful.",
