                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-06-02").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Extension security expert | Point Blanche",
                        Description = "To: Stella.Dagelet@minbzk.nl\nCC: Nathalie.Tackling@sintmaartengov.org; Saskia.Reuver@minbzk.nl; Johishi.Romney@sintmaartengov.org; antonioba@unops.org; juanca@unops.org\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Extension security expert | Point Blanche\nBody:\nDear Stella,\nWith a little bit of delay I hereby formally confirm availability of Ross and that logistical arrangement have been made in order to facilitate his support to the MInistry of Justice in Sint Maarten,\nAdditionally, I take this opportunity to indicate that as part of the actions taken in response to the present situation, UNOPS has also mobilized Mrs Sofia Trejos, Communication Specialist to support the current efforts of the MoJ from a PR perspective both for the current situation, but also in preparation of the upcoming stages of the project.\nMrs Trejos will be in Philipsburg the week of the 2nd of June.\nAll specific activities conducted as part of this adhoc support will be formally reported upon through an extraordinary IPB.\nKind regards\nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\nHead of Programme | ICMCO | LCR\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154Follow us on social media and subscribe to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\nOn Wed, May 28, 2025 at 1:30 PM Dagelet, Stella <Stella.Dagelet@minbzk.nl> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear William,\n\n\n\n\nFirst of all, we would like to express our sincere appreciation to UNOPS for your flexibility in providing immediate support to assisit Sint Maarten during the crisis in the Point Blanche Prison. The UNOPS engineer and\n the security expert have contributed significantly to the emergency and response measures that Sint Maarten has taken after the fire.\n\n \nSince his arrival last Friday, the safety expert Ross Toomer, has diligently worked with the crisis team on the development of a response plan to safely restore operations at the prison the coming weeks.\nTo further consolidate this response plan, we kindly request an extension of one additional week for the deployment of Ross Toomer to continue working alongside the existing crisis team to fully implement the response\n plan and ensure the situation in Point Blanche is stabilized.\n \nWe look forward to your confirmation of this request.\n \nKind regards,\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nS. (Stella) Dagelet LL.M\nSenior beleidsmedewerker\n........................................................................\n\nVertegenwoordiging van Nederland in Philipsburg \n\nMinisterie van Binnenlandse Zaken en Koninkrijksrelaties\n \nFrontstreet 26 | Philipsburg | Sint Maarten\n\nPostbus 20011 | 2500 EA | Den Haag\n........................................................................\nM: +1 721 581 55 80\nE:\nStella.dagelet@minbzk.nl\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\nDit bericht kan informatie bevatten die niet voor u is bestemd. Indien u niet de geadresseerde bent of dit bericht abusievelijk aan u is toegezonden, wordt u verzocht dat aan de afzender te melden en het bericht te verwijderen. De Staat aanvaardt geen aansprakelijkheid voor schade, van welke aard ook, die verband houdt met risico's verbonden aan het elektronisch verzenden van berichten.\nThis message may contain information that is not intended for you. If you are not the addressee or if this message was sent to you by mistake, you are requested to inform the sender and delete the message. The State accepts no liability for damage of any kind resulting from the risks inherent in the electronic transmission of messages.",
                        Location = null,
                        GmailThreadId = null,
                        GmailMessageId = "00TQx00000Ptdf8MAB",
                        EmailAddresses = new List<string> { "antonioba@unops.org", "juanca@unops.org", "johishi.romney@sintmaartengov.org", "stella.dagelet@minbzk.nl", "saskia.reuver@minbzk.nl", "nathalie.tackling@sintmaartengov.org" },
                        Status = (EntityStatus)1,
