                ),
                new (
                    "00TQx00000PirdOMAR",
                    new UNOPSInteraction
                    {
                        Name = "Email: Re: Official invitation to UNOPS high-level event, “From Resources to Results: Speeding-up Implementation in Middle-Income Countries,”",
                        Type = InteractionType.Email,
                        Date = DateTime.Parse("2025-05-28").ToUniversalTime(),
                        Subject = "Email: Re: Official invitation to UNOPS high-level event, “From Resources to Results: Speeding-up Implementation in Middle-Income Countries,”",
                        Description = "To: williamsg@unops.org\nCC: DBB@sintmaartengov.org; PMCabinet@sintmaartengov.org; antoinel@unops.org; Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org; giuseppem@unops.org; Luc.Mercelina@sintmaartengov.org; Perdeepkoemar.Doekharan@sintmaartengov.org; marc.rooijackers@minbuza.nl\nBCC: \nAttachment: --none--\n\nSubject: Re: Official invitation to UNOPS high-level event, “From Resources to Results: Speeding-up Implementation in Middle-Income Countries,”\nBody:\nDear Mr. Moreira da Silva and Mr. Mancinelli,\n\n\n\n\n\nOn behalf of the Honorable Prime Minister of Sint Maarten, Dr. Luc F. E. Mercelina, I wish to extend sincere appreciation for your kind invitation to participate as a speaker at the UNOPS high-level event, “From Resources to Results: Speeding-up Implementation\n in Middle-Income Countries,” during the Fourth International Conference on Financing for Development (FfD4) in Seville.\n\n\n\n\n\nWhile the Prime Minister is deeply honored to have been considered for such an important engagement, due to pressing obligations during the proposed period, he will regrettably be unable to attend the event in person.\n\n\n\n\n\nNevertheless, Prime Minister Mercelina remains fully supportive of the objectives of this high-level dialogue and recognizes its significance in advancing the global development agenda. We kindly request to be kept informed of the session’s outcomes and express\n the Prime Minister’s interest in exploring future avenues for engagement and collaboration with UNOPS and its partners.\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease accept, the assurances of the Prime Minister’s highest consideration.\n\n\n\n\n\nRegards, \n\n\n\n\n\nStuart Johnson \n\nChief of Staff \n\nHonorable Prime Minister Dr. Luc Mercelina  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom: William SQUIER GONZALEZ <williamsg@unops.org>\n\nSent: Tuesday, May 27, 2025 5:14:08 PM\n\nTo: Johnson, Stuart <Stuart.Johnson@sintmaartengov.org>\n\nCc: DBB <DBB@sintmaartengov.org>; PMCabinet <PMCabinet@sintmaartengov.org>; Antoine LUST <antoinel@unops.org>; Gumbs, Angelique <Angelique.Gumbs@sintmaartengov.org>; Giuseppe MANCINELLI <giuseppem@unops.org>\n\nSubject: Re: Official invitation to UNOPS high-level event, “From Resources to Results: Speeding-up Implementation in Middle-Income Countries,”\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou don't often get email from williamsg@unops.org. \nLearn why this is important \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDear Chief of Staff Stuart Johnson,\n\n\n\nOn behalf of UNOPS Executive Director Jorge Moreira Da Silva and, Deputy Regional Director for Latin America and the Caribbean Giuseppe Mancinelli, allow me to kindly follow up on our previous email and reiterate our interest in having the Government\n of Sint Maarten represented in this High-level event curated by UNOPS.\n\n\n\nKind regards\n\n\n\n\nWilliam SQUIER GONZALEZ\n\nHead of Programme | ICMCO | LCR\n\nSan Jose, Costa Rica | Tel: +506 8337 9154\n\n\nFollow us\n on social media and subscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOn Tue, 20 May 2025 at 6:46 PM Giuseppe MANCINELLI <giuseppem@unops.org> wrote:\n\n\n\n\n\nYour Excellency,\nI hope this message finds you well.\nOn behalf of Mr. Jorge Moreira da Silva, United Nations Under-Secretary-General and Executive Director of UNOPS, I am pleased to extend to you an official invitation to participate as a distinguished speaker at the UNOPS high-level event,\n“From Resources to Results: Speeding-up Implementation in Middle-Income Countries,” to be held during the Fourth International Conference on Financing for Development (FfD4), in\nSeville, Spain, at the FIBES Sevilla Exhibition and Conference Centre, in\nJune–July 2025 (exact date to be confirmed).\nThe event—pending final approval by the conference organizers—will focus on overcoming the challenges of turning financing commitments into tangible outcomes in low- and middle-income countries. The session will explore practical strategies to enhance implementation\n capacity, accelerate project delivery, and foster effective partnerships aligned with the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development.\nGiven your exemplary leadership as Prime Minister of Sint Maarten, we would be truly honoured to benefit from your insights and experiences in this dialogue. Other confirmed speakers include senior representatives from the Government of Montenegro and the\n European Investment Bank.\nPlease find the official letter of invitation from Mr. Moreira da Silva attached for your reference.\nShould you have any questions or require further details, we remain at your full disposal and would be happy to assist.\nWe very much hope you will be able to join us for this important exchange and look forward to your response.\nWith highest regards,\nG.\n\n\n\n\n\nGiuseppe Mancinelli\n| Deputy Director,\nLatin America and the Caribbean Regional Office\n| Representative Mexico | Mexico City\n | Tel: +52 56 34098181 | Follow\n us on social media and\nsubscribe\n to our newsletter. | www.unops.org\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.",
